EXAM_DATA.papers["2021-english-one"] = {"id":"2021-english-one","year":2021,"label":"2021 英语一","era":"modern","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2021-english-one/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"estimated","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"Fluid intelligence is the type of intelligence that has to do with short-term memory and the ability to think quickly, logically, and abstractly in order to solve new problems. It   {{1}}   in young adulthood, levels out for a period of time, and then   {{2}}   starts to slowly decline as we age. But   {{3}}   aging is inevitable, scientists are finding out that certain changes in brain function may not be."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"One study found that muscle loss and the   {{4}}   of body fat around the abdomen are associated with a decline in fluid intelligence. This suggests the   {{5}}   that lifestyle factors might help prevent or   {{6}}   this type of decline."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"The researchers looked at data that   {{7}}   measurements of lean muscle and abdominal fat from more than 4,000 middle- to older-aged men and women and   {{8}}   that data to reported changes in fluid intelligence over a six-year period. They found that middle-aged people   {{9}}   higher measures of abdominal fat   {{10}}   worse on measures of fluid intelligence as the years   {{11}}   ."},{"id":"p-section1-4","text":"For women, the association may be   {{12}}   to changes in immunity that resulted from excess abdominal fat; in men, the immune system did not appear to be   {{13}}   . It is hoped that future studies could   {{14}}   these differences and perhaps lead to different   {{15}}   for men and women."},{"id":"p-section1-5","text":"{{16}}   there are steps you can   {{17}}   to help reduce abdominal fat and maintain lean muscle mass as you age in order to protect both your physical and mental   {{18}}   . The two highly recommended lifestyle approaches are maintaining or increasing your   {{19}}   of aerobic exercise and following a Mediterranean-style   {{20}}   that is high in fiber and eliminates highly processed foods."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"pauses"},{"key":"B","text":"returns"},{"key":"C","text":"peaks"},{"key":"D","text":"fades"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"1.","reason":"三段式趋势：先升、再平、后降 线索就在本句的并列结构 It __(1)__ in young adulthood, levels out for a period of time, and then __(2)__ starts to slowly decline as we age：后面明说「持平一段时间」再「缓慢下降」，那么青年期这第一阶段必然是趋势的最高点，答案应具备「达到顶峰」的语义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"pauses 是「暂停」，与后文「持平再下降」的升—平—降曲线对不上，青年期是上升到顶而非中途停顿。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"returns 是「返回、回到」，文中并无智力先降后回的前提，逻辑上无处可「返回」。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"peaks 意为「达到顶峰」，正好对应「青年期最高—持平—后降」的三段曲线，与 levels out for a period of time, and then __(2)__ starts to slowly decline 形成完整趋势。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"fades 是「衰退」，若青年期就衰退，则与后文 starts to slowly decline 重复且把曲线变成一路下滑，与「持平」阶段矛盾。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"alternatively"},{"key":"B","text":"formally"},{"key":"C","text":"accidentally"},{"key":"D","text":"generally"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"as we age 表明是普遍随龄规律 本句尾的 starts to slowly decline as we age 点出这是「随着年龄增长」普遍发生的过程，答案应具备「通常、一般而言」这种概括性，而非偶然或正式。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"alternatively 用于给出另一种选择，句中并无两种可选方案的对照，语义无处落脚。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"formally 指形式上、官方地，与智力的生理性下降毫无关联。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"accidentally 是「偶然地」，但 as we age 说明下降是人人随龄都会发生的普遍现象，并非偶发。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"generally 的「一般地、普遍地」恰好概括 as we age 这一随龄普遍规律，与全句客观陈述的语气一致。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"while"},{"key":"B","text":"since"},{"key":"C","text":"once"},{"key":"D","text":"until"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"3.","reason":"「不可避免」对「未必如此」的对比 线索是两分句的对立：前句 aging is inevitable 说衰老不可避免，后句 certain changes in brain function may not be（may not be inevitable）说脑功能变化未必不可避免，二者构成「尽管……却……」的让步对比，答案应是让步/对比连词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"while 在此引导让步状语从句「虽然衰老不可避免」，与主句「脑功能变化却未必」形成对比，恰好承接前面的 But 强化转折语气。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"since 表原因「既然、因为」，但「衰老不可避免」并不是「脑功能变化未必」的原因，两句是对比而非因果。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"once 表「一旦……就」，引入时间或条件，但两句并无「先衰老、后变化」的时间触发关系。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"until 表「直到……为止」，句中没有时间终点关系，代入语义不通。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"detection"},{"key":"B","text":"accumulation"},{"key":"C","text":"consumption"},{"key":"D","text":"separation"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"与 muscle loss 并列、共同导致衰退 线索在并列主语 muscle loss and the __(4)__ of body fat around the abdomen are associated with a decline in fluid intelligence：muscle loss（肌肉流失）是负面变化，与它并列、共同关联到智力衰退的脂肪状态，应是脂肪的「增多、堆积」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"detection 指检测脂肪的行为，但本句谈的是脂肪本身的状态与智力衰退相关，不是检测动作。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"accumulation 意为「积累、堆积」，与 muscle loss 并列同为负面变化，正好是导致 a decline in fluid intelligence 的脂肪过多状态。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"consumption 指消耗脂肪，方向与「肌肉流失同向的负面变化」相反，脂肪消耗一般是有益的，逻辑不合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"separation 是「分离、分开」，与腹部脂肪不构成有意义的搭配，语义落空。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"possibility"},{"key":"B","text":"decision"},{"key":"C","text":"goal"},{"key":"D","text":"requirement"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"5.","reason":"suggests + might 表推测、未定论 线索是动词与情态词 This suggests the __(5)__ that lifestyle factors might help prevent or __(6)__ this type of decline：suggests（暗示）与 might（也许）都是不确定语气，研究只是提出一种「可能性」，而非已定的决定、目标或要求。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"possibility 表「可能性」，与 suggests 和 might help 的推测语气完全一致，研究提出生活方式或许能干预衰退的可能。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"decision 是「决定」，需要主体作出选择，但句中是研究数据的推测，不是谁作的决定。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"goal 是「目标」，而 might help 表达的是不确定的可能而非设定的目标，语气不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"requirement 是「要求、必需」，断言过强，与 suggests／might 的试探语气冲突。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"delay"},{"key":"B","text":"ensure"},{"key":"C","text":"seek"},{"key":"D","text":"utilize"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"6.","reason":"与 prevent 并列、对象是「衰退」 线索是并列伙伴和共同宾语 prevent or __(6)__ this type of decline：prevent（预防）是对衰退的正面干预，or 连接的本空应与之同向——也是减轻衰退后果的动作，即「延缓」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"delay 意为「延缓、推迟」，与 prevent 并列，构成「预防或延缓这种衰退」，都是对抗衰退的正向干预，语义贴切。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"ensure 是「确保」，「确保衰退」与 prevent 方向相反，逻辑荒谬。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"seek 是「寻求、追求」，「寻求衰退」与生活方式的有益作用矛盾。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"utilize 是「利用」，「利用这种衰退」搭配不当，也与正向干预的语境相悖。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"modified"},{"key":"B","text":"supported"},{"key":"C","text":"included"},{"key":"D","text":"predicted"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"7.","reason":"数据「含有」各项测量值 线索是主宾本身 data that __(7)__ measurements of lean muscle and abdominal fat from more than 4,000 ... men and women：研究者查看的数据里「装着」这四千多人的肌肉与脂肪测量值，data 与 measurements 是「包含」关系。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"modified 是「修改」，数据修改测量值没有事实依据，研究只是查看现成数据。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"supported 是「支持」，常用于数据支持某结论，而此处宾语是 measurements（测量值本身），数据「支持测量值」不通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"included 意为「包含」，数据集里包含肌肉与脂肪的测量值，data that __(7)__ measurements 主宾关系朴素准确。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"predicted 是「预测」，数据预测的应是未来结果，而非其自身已有的测量值，逻辑错位。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"devoted"},{"key":"B","text":"compared"},{"key":"C","text":"converted"},{"key":"D","text":"applied"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"8.","reason":"把脂肪数据「对照」智力变化 线索是整句研究逻辑 looked at data that __(7)__ measurements ... and __(8)__ that data to reported changes in fluid intelligence：研究者拿测量数据去和「报告中的智力变化」相互对照，从而发现相关性，动作应是「比较、对照」，且 compare ... to 搭配成立。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"devoted 虽能接 to，但 devote data to 意为「把数据献给／投入于」，与「找关联」的研究动作不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"compared 与 to 构成 compare ... to「将……与……作比较」，正好描述把脂肪测量值同智力变化对照以发现相关性，搭配与语义双对。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"converted 是「转换、转化」，把测量数据「转换为」智力变化不符合研究实际，二者是对照关系而非转化关系。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"applied 与 to 搭配表「把……应用于」，但研究并非把数据应用于智力变化，而是两相比较，语义不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"with"},{"key":"B","text":"above"},{"key":"C","text":"by"},{"key":"D","text":"against"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"9.","reason":"people ___ higher fat 表「拥有较高脂肪的人」 线索就在本句结构 middle-aged people __(9)__ higher measures of abdominal fat：要表达「腹部脂肪测量值较高的中年人」，即「人 + 具有 + 某属性」，英语用介词 with（with higher measures of fat）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"with 表「带有、具有」，people __(9)__ higher measures of abdominal fat 即「腹部脂肪较高的人」，是表属性的标准搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"above 表位置或数值「高于」某基准，需有比较对象，「people above higher measures」逻辑不成立。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"by 表凭借、方式或差额，无法表达「人具有某属性」，与本句结构不配。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"against 表「反对、逆着」，「人对抗较高脂肪」与原意（拥有较高脂肪）相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lived"},{"key":"B","text":"managed"},{"key":"C","text":"scored"},{"key":"D","text":"played"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"10.","reason":"score worse on measures 表「测试得分更差」 线索是本句搭配框架 __(10)__ worse on measures of fluid intelligence：与表现好坏（worse）和测验（on measures）连用、表「在测试中得分如何」的动词是 score，固定搭配 score well/worse on (a test)。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"lived 是「生活」，与 worse on measures of fluid intelligence 无法构成「测验表现」的搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"managed 表「设法、管理」，不能搭配 worse on measures 表示在测试中得分高低。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"scored 与 worse on measures 构成 score worse on「在……测验中得分更差」，__(10)__ worse on measures of fluid intelligence 是地道固定搭配。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"played 是「玩、参加比赛」，虽能说 played worse，但其对象通常是运动比赛，与 measures of fluid intelligence（智力测验）不配。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ran out"},{"key":"B","text":"set off"},{"key":"C","text":"drew in"},{"key":"D","text":"went by"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"11.","reason":"六年期 → years went by 表「岁月流逝」 线索结合上文 reported changes in fluid intelligence over a six-year period 与本句 as the years __(11)__：研究跨六年观察智力变化，as 引导的时间状语应表「随着岁月流逝」，固定短语 years go by。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"ran out 是「用尽」，常用于资源耗尽，「岁月用尽」不符合随时间观察的中性语境。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"set off 是「出发、引爆」，与 years 主语搭配无意义。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"drew in 常指白昼变短、夜色降临，不表「岁月流逝」的整体时间推移，语义偏窄不合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"went by 与 years 构成 years go by「岁月流逝、时间过去」，呼应 over a six-year period 的纵向观察，搭配地道。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"superior"},{"key":"B","text":"attributable"},{"key":"C","text":"parallel"},{"key":"D","text":"resistant"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"12.","reason":"association 由免疫变化「导致」→ 归因 线索是主语与从句的因果 the association may be __(12)__ to changes in immunity that resulted from excess abdominal fat：「相关性」可能源于「免疫变化」，且免疫变化又由脂肪过多引起，整条因果链要求本空表「可归因于」，即 be attributable to。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"superior 接 to 表「比……优越」，与「相关性归因于免疫变化」的因果含义无关。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"attributable 接 to 构成 be attributable to「可归因于」，正好表达女性的这种相关性可能源于免疫变化，因果链完整。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"parallel 接 to 表「与……平行、类似」，是并列关系而非因果归因，语义不合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"resistant 接 to 表「对……有抵抗力」，与「相关性源于免疫变化」相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"restored"},{"key":"B","text":"isolated"},{"key":"C","text":"involved"},{"key":"D","text":"controlled"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"13.","reason":"与女性「免疫变化起作用」相对照 线索在分号前后的对比 For women, the association may be __(12)__ to changes in immunity ...; in men, the immune system did not appear to be __(13)__：女性的相关性涉及免疫变化，而男性「免疫系统似乎没有 ___」，对照之下应表「（免疫）未被牵涉、未参与其中」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"restored 是「恢复」，前文并未谈免疫受损，「免疫系统未被恢复」与对比逻辑不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"isolated 是「被隔离」，与「是否参与该相关性」的对比维度不在一条线上。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"involved 表「被卷入、参与」，与女性免疫「起了作用」恰成对照——男性的免疫系统似乎未参与其中，the immune system did not appear to be __(13)__ 对比工整。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"controlled 是「被控制」，文中不涉及对免疫系统的控制，无法与女性免疫起作用形成对照。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"alter"},{"key":"B","text":"spread"},{"key":"C","text":"remove"},{"key":"D","text":"explain"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"14.","reason":"研究的目的是弄清差异、进而指导用药 线索是目的状语 future studies could __(14)__ these differences and perhaps lead to different __(15)__ for men and women：研究先「搞清楚」这些男女差异，才可能据此提出不同对策，故动作应是「解释、阐明」差异，而非改变或消除它。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"alter 是「改变」，研究的任务是认识差异而非改变这些客观差异，与目的不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"spread 是「传播」，「研究传播这些差异」语义不通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"remove 是「消除」，研究并非要抹去男女差异，而是理解它，方向错误。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"explain 意为「解释、阐明」，未来研究有望弄清男女间的这些差异，进而 lead to different __(15)__ for men and women，逻辑顺承。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"compensations"},{"key":"B","text":"symptoms"},{"key":"C","text":"demands"},{"key":"D","text":"treatments"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"15.","reason":"全文落点是「如何应对衰退」的对策 线索结合主旨与本句 lead to different __(15)__ for men and women：全文谈的是防治流体智力衰退，研究弄清男女差异后顺理成章给出「不同的治疗/干预方案」，答案应属医疗对策类。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"compensations 多指补偿金或代偿，与「针对衰退的医疗方案」不在同一话题域。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"symptoms 是「症状」，是疾病的表现而非研究带来的解决办法，与 lead to（带来）的积极指向不合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"demands 是「要求、需求」，研究弄清差异后产出的应是应对方案，而非「不同的需求」，逻辑偏。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"treatments 意为「治疗、疗法」，与全文健康干预主题一致，研究弄清男女差异后给出不同治疗方案，different __(15)__ for men and women 顺承自然。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Likewise"},{"key":"B","text":"Meanwhile"},{"key":"C","text":"Therefore"},{"key":"D","text":"Instead"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"16.","reason":"机制未明 vs 已有可行步骤，平行推进 线索是上段结尾与本段开头的关系 It is hoped that future studies could __(14)__ these differences 对 __(16)__ there are steps you can __(17)__ to help reduce abdominal fat：上段说男女机制尚待未来研究厘清，本段转而说「与此同时，眼下已有一些可行的步骤」，二者是并行补充（机制待研究，但行动可先行），宜用表「与此同时」的副词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Likewise 表「同样、类似地」，要求前后是同类情形，但上文是「研究展望」、下文是「行动建议」，并非同类，套不上。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Meanwhile 表「与此同时、另一方面」，恰好衔接「机制仍待研究」与「眼下已有可行步骤」这两件并存之事，过渡自然。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Therefore 表「因此」，但「有可行步骤」并非「研究厘清差异」推出的结论，二者非因果关系。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Instead 表「而不是、取而代之」，需前后构成替代否定关系，但本段并非否定上段、另提替代，逻辑不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"change"},{"key":"B","text":"watch"},{"key":"C","text":"count"},{"key":"D","text":"take"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"17.","reason":"take steps 表「采取措施」 线索是动宾框架 there are steps you can __(17)__ to help reduce abdominal fat：要表达「你可以采取一些步骤／措施来减脂」，与 steps 搭配的固定动词是 take（take steps to do）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"change 是「改变」，change steps 不构成「采取措施」之意，与 to help reduce fat 的目的不配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"watch 与 steps 连用多指「当心脚下」，并非「采取行动」，语义错位。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"count 与 steps 连用是「数步数」，与「采取措施减脂」无关。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"take 与 steps 构成 take steps「采取措施／步骤」，steps you can __(17)__ to help reduce abdominal fat 是地道固定搭配。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"well-being"},{"key":"B","text":"process"},{"key":"C","text":"formation"},{"key":"D","text":"coordination"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"18.","reason":"protect physical and mental ___ → 保护身心健康 线索是动词与修饰语 to protect both your physical and mental __(18)__：要表「保护你身体和心理两方面」，被保护的应是「健康／福祉」这一整体状态，well-being 正表此意。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"well-being 意为「健康、安康、福祉」，与 physical and mental 完美搭配，正是要保护的「身心健康」，呼应全文护脑护身的主旨。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"process 是「过程」，「保护身心过程」语义空泛、不通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"formation 是「形成、构成」，与「保护身心」搭配不当。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"coordination 是「协调（性）」，虽与身体相关，但「保护身心协调」并非文意所指的整体健康。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"level"},{"key":"B","text":"love"},{"key":"C","text":"knowledge"},{"key":"D","text":"space"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"19.","reason":"maintain or increase 要求可增减的「量/水平」 线索是动词与搭配 maintaining or increasing your __(19)__ of aerobic exercise：能被「保持或增加」、且与「有氧运动」连用的应是运动的「量、水平」，即 level of exercise（运动量／运动水平）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"level 与 of aerobic exercise 构成 level of exercise「运动水平／运动量」，可被 maintain or increase（保持或增加），搭配与语义双对。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"love 是「热爱」，「增加对有氧运动的热爱」虽勉强可读，但建议针对的是可量化的运动量，不是情感，且后文 high in fiber 等都谈具体量度。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"knowledge 是「知识」，减脂建议要的是增加运动量而非运动知识，偏离实操指向。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"space 是「空间」，与 of aerobic exercise 搭配无意义。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"design"},{"key":"B","text":"routine"},{"key":"C","text":"diet"},{"key":"D","text":"prescription"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"20.","reason":"high in fiber + eliminates processed foods → 饮食 线索是定语从句的内容 a Mediterranean-style __(20)__ that is high in fiber and eliminates highly processed foods：「高纤维、剔除高度加工食品」描述的全是吃的内容，加上 follow a Mediterranean diet 的固定说法，答案应是 diet（饮食、膳食）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"design 是「设计」，「遵循一种地中海式设计」与高纤维、少加工食品的饮食内容不配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"routine 是「日常惯例」，过于宽泛，无法精准表达由 fiber、processed foods 所限定的「饮食」，且 Mediterranean diet 才是固定说法。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"diet 意为「饮食、膳食」，与 Mediterranean-style 构成固定的「地中海饮食」，且其后定语 high in fiber and eliminates highly processed foods 全在描述吃什么，完全吻合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"prescription 是「药方、处方」，本句谈的是日常膳食而非医生开的药方，语义不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"How can the train operators possibly justify yet another increase to rail passenger fares? It has become a grimly reliable annual ritual: every January the cost of travelling by train rises, imposing a significant extra burden on those who have no option but to use the rail network to get to work or otherwise. This year's rise, an average of 2.7 per cent, may be a fraction lower than last year's, but it is still well above the official Consumer Price Index (CPI) measure of inflation."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"Successive governments have permitted such increases on the grounds that the cost of investing in and running the rail network should be borne by those who use it, rather than the general taxpayer. Why, the argument goes, should a car-driving pensioner from Lincolnshire have to subsidise the daily commute of a stockbroker from Surrey? Equally, there is a sense that the travails of commuters in the South East, many of whom will face among the biggest rises, have received too much attention compared to those who must endure the relatively poor infrastructure of the Midlands and the North."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"However, over the past 12 months, those commuters have also experienced some of the worst rail strikes in years. It is all very well train operators trumpeting the improvements they are making to the network, but passengers should be able to expect a basic level of service for the substantial sums they are now paying to travel. The responsibility for the latest wave of strikes rests on the unions. However, there is a strong case that those who have been worst affected by industrial action should receive compensation for the disruption they have suffered."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"The Government has pledged to change the law to introduce a minimum service requirement so that, even when strikes occur, services can continue to operate. This should form part of a wider package of measures to address the long-running problems on Britain's railways. Yes, more investment is needed, but passengers will not be willing to pay more indefinitely if they must also endure cramped, unreliable services, punctuated by regular chaos when timetables are changed, or planned maintenance is managed incompetently. The threat of nationalisation may have been seen off for now, but it will return with a vengeance if the justified anger of passengers is not addressed in short order."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"The author holds that this year's increase in rail passenger fares____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has kept pace with inflation."},{"key":"B","text":"is a big surprise to commuters."},{"key":"C","text":"remains an unreasonable measure."},{"key":"D","text":"will ease train operators' burden."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者认为今年铁路客运票价的上涨____","choicesZh":{"A":"与通货膨胀保持同步。","B":"让通勤者大感意外。","C":"仍然是一项不合理的措施。","D":"将减轻铁路运营商的负担。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author holds that this year's increase in rail passenger fares____ 不含 infer/imply 等推断信号，问的是作者对一项已知事实（涨价）的具体评价，落点在原文具体一句话上。","parse":"The author holds that this year's increase in rail passenger fares____ 是一个待补全的主从复合句，主句 The author holds that... 引出宾语从句，从句主语是 this year's increase in rail passenger fares，谓语缺失（由选项补足）。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"This year's rise, an average of 2.7 per cent, may be a fraction lower than last year's, but it is still well above the official Consumer Price Index (CPI) measure of inflation.","locateZh":"今年涨幅平均 2.7%，可能比去年略低，但仍远高于官方消费者物价指数（CPI）所衡量的通胀水平。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"has kept pace with inflation 意为\"与通胀同步\"，但原文明说 it is still well above the official Consumer Price Index (CPI) measure of inflation，是超过通胀而非同步，方向完全相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"is a big surprise to commuters 把涨价说成\"对通勤者是大惊喜\"，但原文将涨价称为 a grimly reliable annual ritual（一年一度可预料的惯例），恰恰是\"毫不意外\"，文中并无 surprise 语义。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判到\"涨幅超通胀、不合理\"后，扫四个选项只有 remains an unreasonable measure 同时覆盖\"持续状态\"和\"不合理\"两个语义点。","pairs":[{"orig":"it is still well above the official Consumer Price Index (CPI) measure of inflation","opt":"remains an unreasonable measure"},{"orig":"How can the train operators possibly justify yet another increase to rail passenger fares?","opt":"remains an unreasonable measure"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"will ease train operators' burden 意为\"减轻运营商负担\"，但原文 imposing a significant extra burden on those who have no option but to use the rail network 明说负担是加在乘客头上而非运营商；主语张冠李戴。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"The stockbroker in Paragraph 2 is used to stand for____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"car drivers."},{"key":"B","text":"rail travelers."},{"key":"C","text":"local investors."},{"key":"D","text":"ordinary taxpayers."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"第2段中的股票经纪人被用来代表____","choicesZh":{"A":"汽车驾驶者。","B":"铁路旅客。","C":"本地投资者。","D":"普通纳税人。"},"analysis":{"type":"The stockbroker in Paragraph 2 is used to stand for____ 问的是这一举例在论证中代表哪一类人，是典型的例证目的题。","parse":"The stockbroker in Paragraph 2 is used to stand for____ 主干 The stockbroker is used to stand for + 宾语；被动结构 is used to 表示\"被用来\"，stand for 意为\"代表/代指\"。后置定语 in Paragraph 2 限定指代位置。结构清晰、无陷阱。","locateEn":"Why, the argument goes, should a car-driving pensioner from Lincolnshire have to subsidise the daily commute of a stockbroker from Surrey?","locateZh":"（这种论调说）凭什么让一个来自林肯郡、自己开车的退休老人，去补贴一个来自萨里郡的股票经纪人的日常通勤？","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"car drivers 在 P2 对比中对应的是 a car-driving pensioner from Lincolnshire，即 stockbroker 的对立面（出钱补贴方）而非 stockbroker 自己。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"P2 的整段论证是\"为什么应由 rail 用户付钱而不是普通纳税人\"，对比句中 stockbroker 代表\"用车一方\"，即铁路通勤者，B 项 rail travelers 精准命中。","pairs":[{"orig":"the daily commute of a stockbroker from Surrey","opt":"rail travelers"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"local investors 意为\"当地投资者\"，但 P2 通篇未涉及 invest as 投资行为；文中 cost of investing in ... the rail network 的 invest 是政府/纳税人对铁路网的投入，与 stockbroker 的金融职业无关。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"ordinary taxpayers 对应原文 the general taxpayer，但 general taxpayer 是 stockbroker 的对立面（被对比为出钱方），不是 stockbroker 本人代表的对象。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"It is indicated in Paragraph 3 that train operators____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"are offering compensation to commuters."},{"key":"B","text":"are trying to repair relations with the unions."},{"key":"C","text":"have failed to provide an adequate service."},{"key":"D","text":"have suffered huge losses owing to the strikes."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"第3段指出铁路运营商____","choicesZh":{"A":"正在向通勤者提供补偿。","B":"正在努力修复与工会的关系。","C":"未能提供充分的服务。","D":"因罢工遭受了巨额损失。"},"analysis":{"type":"It is indicated in Paragraph 3 that train operators____ 中 indicated 指文中已明说之事，要找原文一句明示性表述，按细节题处理。","parse":"It is indicated in Paragraph 3 that train operators____ 形式主语 it 句型，真正主语是 that 从句；从句主语 train operators，谓语由选项补足。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"It is all very well train operators trumpeting the improvements they are making to the network, but passengers should be able to expect a basic level of service for the substantial sums they are now paying to travel.","locateZh":"运营商大肆宣扬他们对铁路网做的改进，这固然不错，但乘客花了如此高的费用出行，理应能期待一个最基本的服务水准。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"are offering compensation to commuters 称运营商正在提供补偿，但原文是作者主张 there is a strong case that those who have been worst affected by industrial action should receive compensation——should receive 是\"应该收到\"，即\"目前没收到、作者建议应该收到\"，与 are offering 的现在进行时方向相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"are trying to repair relations with the unions 称运营商在修复与工会的关系，但 P3 通篇未提运营商与工会的关系修复，只说 The responsibility for the latest wave of strikes rests on the unions——把责任归在工会，并未谈关系修复。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判到\"运营商未提供基本服务\"后，扫四个选项只有 have failed to provide an adequate service 与之同义；其余三项各有方向性偏差。","pairs":[{"orig":"passengers should be able to expect a basic level of service for the substantial sums they are now paying to travel","opt":"have failed to provide an adequate service"},{"orig":"the worst rail strikes in years","opt":"have failed to provide an adequate service"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"have suffered huge losses owing to the strikes 说运营商因罢工蒙受巨大损失，但 P3 通篇讲乘客（commuters）受罢工影响、应受补偿，从未谈到运营商自身的损失。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"If unable to calm down passengers, the railways may have to face____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the loss of investment."},{"key":"B","text":"the collapse of operations."},{"key":"C","text":"a reduction of revenue."},{"key":"D","text":"a change of ownership."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"如果无法安抚乘客,铁路可能不得不面对____","choicesZh":{"A":"投资的流失。","B":"运营的崩溃。","C":"收入的减少。","D":"所有权的变更。"},"analysis":{"type":"If unable to calm down passengers, the railways may have to face____ 问的是原文已明说的一种可能后果，答案在原文必有直接对应句，按细节题处理。","parse":"If unable to calm down passengers, the railways may have to face____ 主干 the railways may have to face + 宾语；If unable to calm down passengers 是省略主语和系动词的条件状语从句（完整应为 If the railways are unable to calm down passengers）。calm down passengers 意为\"安抚旅客（的怒气）\"。","locateEn":"The threat of nationalisation may have been seen off for now, but it will return with a vengeance if the justified anger of passengers is not addressed in short order.","locateZh":"国有化的威胁眼下也许已被击退，但若不尽快回应乘客那合情合理的愤怒，它将卷土重来。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"the loss of investment 称投资流失，但原文 more investment is needed 只说还需要更多投资，并未说不安抚乘客就会失去投资；选项偏离题干问的\"将面临什么\"主线。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the collapse of operations 称运营崩溃，但原文只警告国有化威胁回归，并未推及运营崩溃这一更极端后果；考生若把\"不安抚→崩溃\"直接连起来，已超出文本支持的范围。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"a reduction of revenue 称收入减少，文中虽提到 passengers will not be willing to pay more indefinitely，但\"不愿继续付钱\"≠\"收入会减少\"——这中间还有诸多变量；原文未明示收入这一后果。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判国有化即所有权变更后，扫四个选项只有 a change of ownership 命中这一抽象含义；其余三项均为周边干扰。","pairs":[{"orig":"The threat of nationalisation ... will return with a vengeance","opt":"a change of ownership"}]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Who Are to Blame for the Strikes?"},{"key":"B","text":"Constant Complaining Doesn't Work"},{"key":"C","text":"Can Nationalisation Bring Hope?"},{"key":"D","text":"Ever-rising Fares Aren't Sustainable"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"以下哪项最适合作为本文的标题?","choicesZh":{"A":"谁该为罢工负责?","B":"不断抱怨不起作用","C":"国有化能带来希望吗?","D":"不断上涨的票价难以为继"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text? 是主旨题——标题必须覆盖全文，而不能只对应某一段。","parse":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text? 主语是 Which，谓语 would be，表语 the best title for the text。情态动词 would 表委婉语气，无实义。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Who Are to Blame for the Strikes? 只对应 P3 关于罢工责任 The responsibility for the latest wave of strikes rests on the unions 的局部讨论，根本未触及全文主线（涨价不可持续）。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Constant Complaining Doesn't Work 称\"抱怨没有用\"，但全文是作者本人在批评涨价、为乘客发声，立场是 the justified anger of passengers（乘客愤怒合情合理），从未贬低抱怨。该标题与作者立场完全反向。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Can Nationalisation Bring Hope? 把国有化框成\"希望\"，但 P4 末句 The threat of nationalisation ... will return with a vengeance 用 threat 和 with a vengeance（凶猛地、报复性地）的负面色彩词把国有化定性为威胁，绝非希望。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 项 Ever-rising Fares Aren't Sustainable 同时覆盖 P1 涨价不合理、P3 价高服务差、P4 警告国有化卷土重来——四段全部落到\"涨价不可持续\"这一主线。","pairs":[{"orig":"How can the train operators possibly justify yet another increase to rail passenger fares?","opt":"Ever-rising Fares Aren't Sustainable"},{"orig":"passengers will not be willing to pay more indefinitely","opt":"Ever-rising Fares Aren't Sustainable"},{"orig":"The threat of nationalisation ... will return with a vengeance","opt":"Ever-rising Fares Aren't Sustainable"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"Last year marked the third year in a row that Indonesia's bleak rate of deforestation has slowed in pace. One reason for the turnaround may be the country's antipoverty program."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"In 2007, Indonesia started phasing in a program that gives money to its poorest residents under certain conditions, such as requiring people to keep kids in school or get regular medical care. Called conditional cash transfers or CCTs, these social assistance programs are designed to reduce inequality and break the cycle of poverty. They're already used in dozens of countries worldwide. In Indonesia, the program has provided enough food and medicine to substantially reduce severe growth problems among children."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"But CCT programs don't generally consider effects on the environment. In fact, poverty alleviation and environmental protection are often viewed as conflicting goals, says Paul Ferraro, an economist at Johns Hopkins University."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"That's because economic growth can be correlated with environmental degradation, while protecting the environment is sometimes correlated with greater poverty. However, those correlations don't prove cause and effect. The only previous study analyzing causality, based on an area in Mexico that had instituted CCTs, supported the traditional view. There, as people got more money, some of them may have more cleared land for cattle to raise for meat, Ferraro says."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"Such programs do not have to negatively affect the environment, though. Ferraro wanted to see if Indonesia's poverty-alleviation program was affecting deforestation. Indonesia has the third-largest area of tropical forest in the world and one of the highest deforestation rates."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-6","text":"Ferraro analyzed satellite data showing annual forest loss from 2008 to 2012—including during Indonesia's phase-in of the antipoverty program—in 7,468 forested villages across 15 provinces. \"We see that the program is associated with a 30 percent reduction in deforestation,\" Ferraro says."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-7","text":"That's likely because the rural poor are using the money as makeshift insurance policies against inclement weather, Ferraro says. Typically, if rains are delayed, people may clear land to plant more rice to supplement their harvests."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-8","text":"Whether this research translates elsewhere is anybody's guess. Ferraro suggests the results may transfer to other parts of Asia, due to commonalities such as the importance of growing rice and market access. And regardless of transferability, the study shows that what's good for people may also be good for the environment. Even if this program didn't reduce poverty, Ferraro says, \"the value of the avoided deforestation just for carbon dioxide emissions alone is more than the program costs.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"According to the first two paragraphs, CCT programs aim to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"facilitate healthcare reform."},{"key":"B","text":"help poor families get better off."},{"key":"C","text":"improve local education systems."},{"key":"D","text":"lower deforestation rates."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据前两段,CCT项目旨在____","choicesZh":{"A":"促进医疗改革。","B":"帮助贫困家庭改善生活。","C":"改善地方教育系统。","D":"降低森林砍伐率。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 CCT programs aim to____ 问的是项目的既定目的，这是一个可以在文中直接找到陈述句对应的客观事实，不涉及推断或主旨概括。","parse":"According to the first two paragraphs, CCT programs aim to____ 是一个待补全的陈述句，主干是 \"CCT programs aim to ___\"，需要把选项作为不定式短语接在 to 后面构成完整句意；句首 According to 引出的介词短语只起信息来源限定作用，不进入答案语义。","locateEn":"Called conditional cash transfers or CCTs, these social assistance programs are designed to reduce inequality and break the cycle of poverty.","locateZh":"这些被称为有条件现金转移支付（CCT）的社会援助项目，旨在减少不平等、打破贫困循环。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"facilitate healthcare reform 把 get regular medical care 这个 \"领取现金的条件\" 偷换成了\"项目的目的\"——医疗只是触发现金发放的前提条件，并非 CCT 的设计意图。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判的核心是\"让穷人脱贫\"，B 选项 help poor families get better off 正好完整覆盖该语义，是定位句目的部分的同义替换。","pairs":[{"orig":"break the cycle of poverty","opt":"help poor families get better off"},{"orig":"reduce inequality","opt":"help poor families"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"improve local education systems 同样把发放现金的条件 keep kids in school\"误读成项目目的——\"让孩子留在学校\"是领钱条件，绝不等于\"改善教育系统\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"lower deforestation rates 是文章后半部分（P5–P8）才出现的研究发现，并不在前两段 CCT 的\"设计目的\"陈述范围内；CCT 减少砍伐是研究后的意外发现，并非项目初衷。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"The study based on an area in Mexico is cited to show that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cattle raising has been a major means of livelihood for the poor."},{"key":"B","text":"CCT programs have helped preserve traditional lifestyles."},{"key":"C","text":"antipoverty efforts require the participation of local farmers."},{"key":"D","text":"economic growth tends to cause environmental degradation."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"引用基于墨西哥某地区的研究是为了说明____","choicesZh":{"A":"养牛一直是穷人的主要谋生手段。","B":"CCT项目帮助保留了传统生活方式。","C":"扶贫工作需要当地农民的参与。","D":"经济增长往往会导致环境退化。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The study based on an area in Mexico is cited to show that____ 中的 \"cited to show\" 是例证目的题的标志性句式，要找的是例子服务于哪个论点。","parse":"题干主干 \"The study ... is cited to show that ____\"，被动语态加不定式表目的；空格后接 that 从句，选项须能补成完整宾语从句；\"based on an area in Mexico\" 是修饰 study 的过去分词短语，只起定位作用、不进答案语义。","locateEn":"The only previous study analyzing causality, based on an area in Mexico that had instituted CCTs, supported the traditional view.","locateZh":"此前唯一一项分析因果关系的研究——基于墨西哥某地区已实施的 CCT 项目——支持了传统观点。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"cattle raising has been a major means of livelihood for the poor 抓住了 more cleared land for cattle to raise for meat 这个例子内部的细节，但例证题的答案不在例子里，而在例子所证明的论点上；且原文只说\"有些人可能多清地放牛\"，远未上升到\"主要谋生手段\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"CCT programs have helped preserve traditional lifestyles 中 \"preserve traditional lifestyles\"（保护传统生活方式）在原文及墨西哥例子里完全没有任何对应表述；\"traditional\" 一词的出现纯属利用考生对 the traditional view 中 \"traditional\" 的词形眼熟感行骗。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"antipoverty efforts require the participation of local farmers 谈\"扶贫需要当地农民参与\"，全文从未提及参与方/利益相关者这一维度，更未将其与墨西哥研究挂钩。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"墨西哥研究支撑的论点正是\"经济增长与环境恶化挂钩\"，D 项 economic growth tends to cause environmental degradation 是该论点的同义还原。","pairs":[{"orig":"economic growth can be correlated with environmental degradation","opt":"economic growth tends to cause environmental degradation"},{"orig":"supported the traditional view","opt":"economic growth tends to cause environmental degradation"}]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"In his study about Indonesia, Ferraro intends to find out____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"its acceptance level of CCTs."},{"key":"B","text":"its annual rate of poverty alleviation."},{"key":"C","text":"the relation of CCTs to its forest loss."},{"key":"D","text":"the role of its forests in climate change."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在关于印度尼西亚的研究中,Ferraro意图找出____","choicesZh":{"A":"该国对CCT的接受程度。","B":"该国每年的减贫率。","C":"CCT与该国森林损失的关系。","D":"该国森林在气候变化中的作用。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 In his study about Indonesia, Ferraro intends to find out____ 问的是 Ferraro 这项研究的具体目的，文中必有一句直接陈述，对应可查。","parse":"In his study about Indonesia, Ferraro intends to find out____ 主干 \"Ferraro intends to find out ___\"；介词短语 \"In his study about Indonesia\" 作时间/范围状语，是定位提示；空格后接选项作 find out 的宾语，需要是名词性结构。","locateEn":"Ferraro wanted to see if Indonesia's poverty-alleviation program was affecting deforestation.","locateZh":"Ferraro 想看看印尼的扶贫项目是否在影响森林砍伐。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"its acceptance level of CCTs 谈\"印尼对 CCT 的接受程度\"——全文从未涉及 acceptance/popularity 一类的接受度调研，研究关心的是项目效果而非民众态度。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"its annual rate of poverty alleviation 谈\"年均减贫率\"——原文虽提到 CCT \"substantially reduce severe growth problems\"，但从未量化为年均减贫率，更非 Ferraro 印尼研究的目的。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判的核心是双变量\"CCT ↔ deforestation\"的关系问题，C 项 the relation of CCTs to its forest loss 把两变量及其关系完整对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"Indonesia's poverty-alleviation program","opt":"CCTs"},{"orig":"was affecting deforestation","opt":"the relation of CCTs to its forest loss"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the role of its forests in climate change 谈\"印尼森林在气候变化中的作用\"——climate change 一词全文从未出现；末段虽提到 carbon dioxide emissions，但那是研究价值评估而非研究目的，且未上升到\"气候变化\"层面。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"According to Ferraro, the CCT program in Indonesia is most valuable in that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"it will benefit other Asian countries."},{"key":"B","text":"it will reduce regional inequality."},{"key":"C","text":"it can protect the environment."},{"key":"D","text":"it can benefit grain production."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据Ferraro的观点,印度尼西亚的CCT项目最有价值之处在于____","choicesZh":{"A":"它将使其他亚洲国家受益。","B":"它将减少地区不平等。","C":"它能够保护环境。","D":"它能够使粮食生产受益。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 the CCT program in Indonesia is most valuable in that____ 问该项目最具价值之处，文中应有 Ferraro 的明示评价句直接对应。","parse":"According to Ferraro, the CCT program in Indonesia is most valuable in that____ 句中 \"in that\" 是连词短语，相当于 \"because\"，引导原因状语从句，意味着空格处要填的是\"为什么有价值\"的原因，而非\"价值本身\"的同位语解释——这是基础薄弱考生易踩的小坑。","locateEn":"Even if this program didn't reduce poverty, Ferraro says, \"the value of the avoided deforestation just for carbon dioxide emissions alone is more than the program costs.\"","locateZh":"Ferraro 说，即便这个项目没能减贫，仅就避免森林砍伐带来的二氧化碳减排价值而言，就已经超过了项目本身的成本。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"it will benefit other Asian countries 利用 the results may transfer to other parts of Asia——但原文用 may 和 anybody's guess 表明这只是猜测，且这是\"研究可迁移性\"而非\"项目最有价值之处\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"it will reduce regional inequality 把 reduce inequality 改装为 \"regional inequality\"——原文 inequality 指社会贫富不平等，与\"区域间\"无关，且这是 CCT 的设计目的（见 Q26），并非 Ferraro 评价的\"最有价值之处\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Ferraro 的原话排除\"减贫\"价值后强调环境价值，C 项 it can protect the environment 是该评价的上位概括，完全锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"the value of the avoided deforestation just for carbon dioxide emissions alone is more than the program costs","opt":"it can protect the environment"},{"orig":"what's good for people may also be good for the environment","opt":"it can protect the environment"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"it can benefit grain production 来自 plant more rice to supplement their harvests 的反向误读——原文说的是\"没有 CCT 时人们会清地多种水稻\"，CCT 反而抑制了这种行为；把抑制行为说成\"惠及粮食生产\"，与原文方向相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"What is the text centered on?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The effects of a program."},{"key":"B","text":"The debates over a program."},{"key":"C","text":"The process of a study."},{"key":"D","text":"The transferability of a study."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"本文的中心是什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"一个项目的效果。","B":"围绕一个项目的争论。","C":"一项研究的过程。","D":"一项研究的可推广性。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 What is the text centered on? 直接问全文核心，没有任何具体定位词，属典型主旨题。","parse":"What is the text centered on? 是 wh-疑问句，主干 \"the text is centered on what\"，be centered on 表\"以……为中心\"，结构简单无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"The effects of a program 中 program 指 CCT，effects 覆盖 P5 提问、P6 数据结论、P7 机制解释、P8 价值评估，与各区间贡献完全一致，是主线的上位概括。","pairs":[{"orig":"We see that the program is associated with a 30 percent reduction in deforestation","opt":"The effects of a program"},{"orig":"Ferraro wanted to see if Indonesia's poverty-alleviation program was affecting deforestation","opt":"The effects of a program"},{"orig":"the value of the avoided deforestation just for carbon dioxide emissions alone is more than the program costs","opt":"The effects of a program"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"The debates over a program 提示\"项目的争议/辩论\"——但全文并未呈现支持/反对双方的对立观点，P3 虽提及传统观点认为扶贫与环保冲突，但 Ferraro 用研究直接给出反例，并无围绕\"是否该实行 CCT\"的辩论。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"The process of a study 提示\"一项研究的过程\"——文章的确呈现了研究意图（P5）+ 数据（P6）+ 机制（P7）等研究片段，但 P1–P4 的话题引入、概念定义、传统观点反例都不属于研究过程，且 P8 的价值评估也超出研究过程本身；把全文压缩成\"研究过程\"是局部当全文。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"The transferability of a study 提示\"研究的可迁移性\"——这只在末段 Whether this research translates elsewhere is anybody's guess 一句中被提及，且作者明确说\"是任何人的猜测\"，并非全文中心；把末段一笔带过的支线当主旨，是典型的以偏概全。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"As a historian who's always searching for the text or the image that makes us re-evaluate the past, I've become preoccupied with looking for photographs that show our Victorian ancestors smiling (what better way to shatter the image of 19th-century prudery?). I've found quite a few, and—since I started posting them on Twitter—they have been causing quite a stir. People have been surprised to see evidence that Victorians had fun and could, and did, laugh. They are noting that the Victorians suddenly seem to become more human as the hundred-or-so years that separate us fade away through our common experience of laughter."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"Of course, I need to concede that my collection of 'Smiling Victorians' makes up only a tiny percentage of the vast catalogue of photographic portraiture created between 1840 and 1900, the majority of which show sitters posing miserably and stiffly in front of painted backdrops, or staring absently into the middle distance. How do we explain this trend?"},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"During the 1840s and 1850s, in the early days of photography, exposure times were notoriously long: the daguerreotype photographic method (producing an image on a silvered copper plate) could take several minutes to complete, resulting in blurred images as sitters shifted position or adjusted their limbs. The thought of holding a fixed grin as the camera performed its magical duties was too much to contemplate, and so a non-committal blank stare became the norm."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"But exposure times were much quicker by the 1880s, and the introduction of the Box Brownie and other portable cameras meant that, though slow by today's digital standards, the exposure was almost instantaneous. Spontaneous smiles were relatively easy to capture by the 1890s, so we must look elsewhere for an explanation of why Victorians still hesitated to smile."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"One explanation might be the loss of dignity displayed through a cheesy grin. \"Nature gave us lips to conceal our teeth,\" ran one popular Victorian maxim, alluding to the fact that before the birth of proper dentistry, mouths were often in a shocking state of hygiene. A flashing set of healthy and clean, regular 'pearly whites' was a rare sight in Victorian society, the preserve of the super-rich (and even then, dental hygiene was not guaranteed)."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-6","text":"A toothy grin (especially when there were gaps or blackened gnashers) lacked class: drunks, tramps, and music hall performers might gurn and grin with a smile as wide as Lewis Carroll's gum-exposing Cheshire Cat, but it was not a becoming look for properly bred persons. Even Mark Twain, a man who enjoyed a hearty laugh, said that when it came to photographic portraits there could be \"nothing more damning than a silly, foolish smile fixed forever\"."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, the author's posts on Twitter ____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"changed people's impression of the Victorians."},{"key":"B","text":"highlighted social media's role in Victorian studies."},{"key":"C","text":"re-evaluated the Victorian's notion of public image."},{"key":"D","text":"illustrated the development of Victorian photography."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第一段,作者在Twitter上发布的内容____","choicesZh":{"A":"改变了人们对维多利亚时代人的印象。","B":"凸显了社交媒体在维多利亚研究中的作用。","C":"重新评估了维多利亚时代人关于公众形象的观念。","D":"说明了维多利亚时代摄影的发展。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 According to Paragraph 1, the author's posts on Twitter ____ 让考生在第 1 段里找作者帖子产生的事实结果，不带 infer/suggest 等推断信号。","parse":"According to Paragraph 1, the author's posts on Twitter ____ 是一个 \"状语 + 主语 + 谓语空缺\" 的待补全句，According to Paragraph 1 是状语，the author's posts on Twitter 是主语，后接的选项是其谓语；无从句、无否定，结构平直无陷阱。","locateEn":"People have been surprised to see evidence that Victorians had fun and could, and did, laugh. They are noting that the Victorians suddenly seem to become more human as the hundred-or-so years that separate us fade away through our common experience of laughter.","locateZh":"人们惊讶地看到证据，原来维多利亚人也会享受、会笑、确实笑过。他们注意到，维多利亚人突然变得更像 \"人\" 了——相隔我们一百多年的时空，在共同的笑声体验中消融。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"定位句两次强调读者从惊讶到觉得维多利亚人 become more human，这一 \"从刻板到鲜活\" 的转变正是 A 项 changed people's impression 的精确含义。","pairs":[{"orig":"People have been surprised to see evidence that Victorians had fun","opt":"changed people's impression of the Victorians"},{"orig":"the Victorians suddenly seem to become more human","opt":"changed people's impression of the Victorians"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说作者把照片发到 Twitter 引发关注，从未讨论 social media's role in Victorian studies——\"社交媒体在维多利亚研究中的作用\" 是凭空拔高。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈的是 posts 改变了 \"今人对维多利亚人的印象\"，C 项 re-evaluated the Victorian's notion of public image 把对象偷换成 \"维多利亚人自己的公共形象观念\"——主体错位。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文第 1 段重点谈帖子 \"对人们印象的冲击\"，不谈 the development of Victorian photography；摄影技术演变是 P3P4 才出现的话题，不在第 1 段。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"What does the author say about the Victorian portraits he has collected?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"They are in popular use among historians."},{"key":"B","text":"They are rare among photographs of that age."},{"key":"C","text":"They mirror 19th-century social conventions."},{"key":"D","text":"They show effects of different exposure times."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者对他收集的维多利亚时代肖像照片有何看法?","choicesZh":{"A":"它们在历史学家中广泛使用。","B":"它们在那个年代的照片中很罕见。","C":"它们反映了19世纪的社会习俗。","D":"它们显示了不同曝光时间的效果。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 What does the author say about the Victorian portraits he has collected? 是 \"作者就 X 说了什么\" 的陈述事实型问法。","parse":"What does the author say about the Victorian portraits he has collected? 是一个特殊疑问句，主干是 What does the author say about X；X 部分 the Victorian portraits he has collected 中 he has collected 是省略关系代词 that 的定语从句修饰 portraits，意为 \"他已收集的维多利亚肖像\"，定语从句是这句的唯一结构看点。","locateEn":"Of course, I need to concede that my collection of 'Smiling Victorians' makes up only a tiny percentage of the vast catalogue of photographic portraiture created between 1840 and 1900, the majority of which show sitters posing miserably and stiffly in front of painted backdrops, or staring absently into the middle distance.","locateZh":"当然，我必须承认，我的 \"微笑的维多利亚人\" 收藏只占 1840 至 1900 年间产出的庞大肖像目录的极小比例，其中绝大多数都呈现拍摄者僵硬呆板地站在彩绘背景前、或茫然地凝视远处的中景。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未提及这些照片被 in popular use among historians 历史学家广泛使用——作者只是说自己（一名历史学家）在搜集，未涉及同行使用情况。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"tiny percentage 是数量级最小的修饰语，与 rare 直接同义；定位句还紧接补充 the majority of which show sitters posing miserably and stiffly 反衬出微笑照的罕见，进一步坐实 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"my collection of 'Smiling Victorians' makes up only a tiny percentage of the vast catalogue","opt":"They are rare among photographs of that age"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"题干问的是这批微笑照 \"是什么样的\"，不是问 \"它们反映了什么\"。C 项 mirror 19th-century social conventions 跳到 \"反映社会习俗\"，与题干所问的属性维度不符。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"show effects of different exposure times 把照片属性换成 \"曝光时间影响\"——曝光时间话题确实在 P3P4 出现，但讨论的是 \"为什么僵脸照多\"，与作者的微笑照收藏不挂钩。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"What might have kept the Victorians from smiling for pictures in the 1890s?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Their inherent social sensitiveness."},{"key":"B","text":"Their tension before the camera."},{"key":"C","text":"Their distrust of new inventions."},{"key":"D","text":"Their unhealthy dental condition."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在1890年代,是什么可能使维多利亚时代人在拍照时不露笑容?","choicesZh":{"A":"他们与生俱来的社交敏感性。","B":"他们在镜头前的紧张感。","C":"他们对新发明的不信任。","D":"他们不健康的牙齿状况。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 What might have kept the Victorians from smiling for pictures in the 1890s? 虽用 might，但问的是文中已给出的解释，原文会直接交代原因。","parse":"What might have kept the Victorians from smiling for pictures in the 1890s? 中 might have kept 是 \"might + have done\" 的虚拟/推测完成时，表示对过去的推测；keep sb from doing 是固定搭配，意为 \"阻止某人做某事\"。注意 from smiling 不是否定 smile，整句是问 \"什么阻止了他们笑\"。","locateEn":"One explanation might be the loss of dignity displayed through a cheesy grin. \"Nature gave us lips to conceal our teeth,\" ran one popular Victorian maxim, alluding to the fact that before the birth of proper dentistry, mouths were often in a shocking state of hygiene.","locateZh":"一种解释可能是：露齿傻笑会失体面。当时流行的一句格言说 \"造物给我们嘴唇是为遮住牙齿\"，暗指在正规牙科诞生之前，人们的口腔卫生状况骇人。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Their inherent social sensitiveness 把原因拔高到 \"维多利亚人天生敏感的社会性\"——原文只说 the loss of dignity 这一具体顾虑，没有把它归因于民族性格特征。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文未提维多利亚人在相机前 tension 紧张；只说他们怕失体面、不愿露齿，与 \"紧张\" 是两个心理范畴。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"distrust of new inventions \"不信任新发明\" 在原文毫无依据——文章只把曝光时间问题归到 P3P4 早期技术限制，并未说维多利亚人不信任相机这种新发明。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"定位句给出明确因果：因为牙齿状况差，露齿笑会失体面，所以维多利亚人不笑——这正是 D 项 Their unhealthy dental condition 的内核。","pairs":[{"orig":"mouths were often in a shocking state of hygiene","opt":"Their unhealthy dental condition"},{"orig":"before the birth of proper dentistry","opt":"Their unhealthy dental condition"}]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"Mark Twain is quoted to show that the disapproval of smiles in pictures was____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a deep-root belief."},{"key":"B","text":"a misguided attitude."},{"key":"C","text":"a controversial view."},{"key":"D","text":"a thought-provoking idea."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"引用马克·吐温的话是为了表明对照片中微笑的不赞成是____","choicesZh":{"A":"一种根深蒂固的观念。","B":"一种被误导的态度。","C":"一种有争议的观点。","D":"一种发人深省的想法。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Mark Twain is quoted to show that the disapproval of smiles in pictures was____ 用 \"is quoted to show that\" 明确问 \"引用此人是为了说明什么\"，是典型的例证目的题。","parse":"Mark Twain is quoted to show that the disapproval of smiles in pictures was____ 中 is quoted 是被动语态，\"被引用\"；to show that ... 是不定式作目的状语，that 引导宾语从句；从句主语是 the disapproval of smiles in pictures，谓语 was 后空缺由选项补足。理解关键是把 to show 看作 \"目的\"，问的是 \"引用他的目的是说明 disapproval 是怎样的一种东西\"。","locateEn":"A toothy grin (especially when there were gaps or blackened gnashers) lacked class: drunks, tramps, and music hall performers might gurn and grin with a smile as wide as Lewis Carroll's gum-exposing Cheshire Cat, but it was not a becoming look for properly bred persons. Even Mark Twain, a man who enjoyed a hearty laugh, said that when it came to photographic portraits there could be \"nothing more damning than a silly, foolish smile fixed forever\".","locateZh":"露齿笑（尤其有牙缝或黑牙时）很掉档次：醉汉、流浪汉、音乐厅艺人也许会咧嘴大笑，笑得像刘易斯·卡罗尔笔下露牙龈的柴郡猫一样宽，但这对于教养良好之人并非得体之相。甚至连爱开怀大笑的马克·吐温也说，谈到肖像照，\"再没有什么比一个永远定格的傻里傻气的笑容更糟的了\"。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Even 让步 + Mark Twain 这一爱笑的反例都接受 \"傻笑可耻\" 的观点，说明这种 disapproval 不是某人的偏见而是全社会共享的根深观念，正是 a deep-root belief。","pairs":[{"orig":"Even Mark Twain, a man who enjoyed a hearty laugh, said that ... \"nothing more damning than a silly, foolish smile fixed forever\"","opt":"a deep-root belief"},{"orig":"it was not a becoming look for properly bred persons","opt":"a deep-root belief"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"a misguided attitude 是说这种态度 \"被误导、不正确\"，但作者只在客观陈述维多利亚人的看法，没有贬抑它；说 Mark Twain 等人的态度 \"被误导\" 与原文的中立陈述方向相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"a controversial view \"有争议的观点\" 暗示存在正反两方分歧；原文一面倒地呈现 \"反对露齿微笑\"，没有提及任何持反方观点的声音，谈不上 controversial。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"a thought-provoking idea \"发人深省的想法\" 是把作者的中立举证当作他在赞许马克·吐温的话；原文没有任何句子表达 \"这值得深思\" 的色彩，只是为论证 \"厌笑\" 的普遍性服务。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"Which of the following questions does the text answer?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Why did most Victorians look stern in photographs?"},{"key":"B","text":"Why did the Victorians start to view photographs?"},{"key":"C","text":"What made photography develop in the Victorian period?"},{"key":"D","text":"How did smiling in photographs become a post-Victorian norm?"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"文章回答了以下哪个问题?","choicesZh":{"A":"为什么大多数维多利亚时代人在照片中看起来很严肃?","B":"为什么维多利亚时代人开始观看照片?","C":"是什么使摄影在维多利亚时期得以发展?","D":"在照片中微笑是如何成为维多利亚时代之后的规范的?"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Which of the following questions does the text answer? 让考生回到全文层面找作者要解答的问题，等价于问 \"全文围绕什么展开\"。","parse":"Which of the following questions does the text answer? 是特殊疑问句，主干为 Which questions does the text answer，of the following 是介词短语作 questions 的后置定语；the text 是主语，answer 是谓语。结构简单，重点在理解 \"text answer questions\" 是 \"文章回答问题\" 的拟人表达。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"全文骨架是 \"现象 → 设问 → 多重解释\"，A 项 Why did most Victorians look stern in photographs? 就是把 How do we explain this trend? 翻译成英文 Why 句，完全覆盖文章 5 段中的 4 段，是唯一可作主旨的选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"How do we explain this trend?","opt":"Why did most Victorians look stern in photographs?"},{"orig":"the majority of which show sitters posing miserably and stiffly","opt":"Why did most Victorians look stern in photographs?"},{"orig":"One explanation might be the loss of dignity","opt":"Why did most Victorians look stern in photographs?"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未谈论 the Victorians start to view photographs 维多利亚人 \"开始看照片\" 这件事——文章讨论的是他们怎样 \"被拍\" 和拍出来的神情，不是他们何时开始观看照片。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"What made photography develop in the Victorian period? 把 P3P4 关于摄影技术（曝光时间）的局部讨论当作全文主旨；但这两段只是被作者用来 \"排除掉\" 的一个解释，不是全文中心。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"How did smiling in photographs become a post-Victorian norm? 是问 \"微笑在后维多利亚时代如何变成常态\"——原文只讨论维多利亚时代为什么不笑，没有讲后维多利亚（即维多利亚之后）时代微笑如何成为常态。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"From the early days of broadband, advocates for consumers and web-based companies worried that the cable and phone companies selling broadband connections had the power and incentive to favor affiliated websites over their rivals'. That's why there has been such a strong demand for rules that would prevent broadband providers from picking winners and losers online, preserving the freedom and innovation that have been the lifeblood of the Internet."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"Yet that demand has been almost impossible to fill—in part because of pushback from broadband providers, anti-regulatory conservatives and the courts. A federal appeals court weighed in again Tuesday, but instead of providing a badly needed resolution, it only prolonged the fight. At issue before the U.S. Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit was the latest take of the Federal Communications Commission (FCC) on net neutrality, adopted on a party-line vote in 2017. The Republican-penned order not only eliminated the strict net neutrality rules the FCC had adopted when it had a Democratic majority in 2015, but rejected the commission's authority to require broadband providers to do much of anything. The order also declared that state and local governments couldn't regulate broadband providers either."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"The commission argued that other agencies would protect against anti-competitive behavior, such as a broadband-providing conglomerate like AT&T favoring its own video-streaming service at the expense of Netflix and Apple TV. Yet the FCC also ended the investigations of broadband providers that imposed data caps on their rivals' streaming services but not their own."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"On Tuesday, the appeals court unanimously upheld the 2017 order deregulating broadband providers, citing a Supreme Court ruling from 2005 that upheld a similarly deregulatory move. But Judge Patricia Millett rightly argued in a concurring opinion that \"the result is unhinged from the realities of modern broadband service,\" and said Congress or the Supreme Court could intervene to \"avoid trapping Internet regulation in technological anachronism.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"In the meantime, the court threw out the FCC's attempt to block all state rules on net neutrality, while preserving the commission's power to preempt individual state laws that undermine its order. That means more battles like the one now going on between the Justice Department and California, which enacted a tough net neutrality law in the wake of the FCC's abdication."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"The endless legal battles and back-and-forth at the FCC cry out for Congress to act. It needs to give the commission explicit authority once and for all to bar broadband providers from meddling in the traffic on their network and to create clear rules protecting openness and innovation online."}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"There has long been concern that broadband providers would____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"bring web-based firms under control."},{"key":"B","text":"slow down the traffic on their network."},{"key":"C","text":"show partiality in treating clients."},{"key":"D","text":"intensify competition with their rivals."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"长期以来人们一直担心宽带提供商会____","choicesZh":{"A":"将网络公司置于控制之下。","B":"降低其网络上的流量速度。","C":"在对待客户时表现出偏袒。","D":"加剧与其竞争对手的竞争。"},"analysis":{"type":"There has long been concern that broadband providers would____ 是一个待补全的客观叙述，问的是\"担忧的具体内容是什么\"——指向原文某句客观信息，不带 infer/imply。","parse":"There has long been concern that broadband providers would____ 是 \"There be + 名词 + that 同位语从句\" 结构：concern 是抽象名词，that 后面是它的内容；空格补的是 broadband providers would ____ 这个从句的谓语动词原形。结构平铺，无陷阱。","locateEn":"From the early days of broadband, advocates for consumers and web-based companies worried that the cable and phone companies selling broadband connections had the power and incentive to favor affiliated websites over their rivals'.","locateZh":"从宽带发展早期起，消费者权益倡导者和互联网公司就担心：销售宽带连接的有线电视和电话公司，有权力也有动机偏袒与自己关联的网站，而冷落对手的网站。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"bring web-based firms under control 的意思是\"使互联网公司受其控制\"，但原文 advocates for consumers and web-based companies worried 说的是\"互联网公司\"和\"消费者\"是 worried 的一方，不是被控制的一方；偏袒 ≠ 控制。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"slow down the traffic on their network 描述\"限速\"行为，原文首段并未提及，而是 favor affiliated websites over their rivals'——担忧的是\"偏袒\"而非\"限速\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判说的\"偏袒自家、冷落对手\"就是 show partiality in treating clients 的口语化版本，二者语义同心。","pairs":[{"orig":"favor affiliated websites over their rivals'","opt":"show partiality in treating clients"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"intensify competition with their rivals 说的是宽带商与其\"对手\"竞争加剧，但原文 over their rivals' 中的 rivals 是被偏袒网站的对手（即\"网站\"的对手），不是宽带商自己的对手；且原文是\"差别对待\"而非\"加剧竞争\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"Faced with the demand for net neutrality rules, the FCC____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sticks to an out-of-date order."},{"key":"B","text":"takes an anti-regulatory stance."},{"key":"C","text":"has issued a special resolution."},{"key":"D","text":"has allowed the states to intervene."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"面对网络中立性规则的要求,FCC____","choicesZh":{"A":"坚持一项过时的命令。","B":"采取反监管立场。","C":"已经发布了一项特别决议。","D":"已经允许各州进行干预。"},"analysis":{"type":"Faced with the demand for net neutrality rules, the FCC____ 要回答\"FCC 做了什么动作\"，指向原文一处描述 FCC 立场的客观陈述。","parse":"Faced with the demand for net neutrality rules, the FCC____ 开头的 Faced with 是过去分词作状语，主语仍是 the FCC；空格里要填的是 FCC 的实际行为/态度。结构清晰，无陷阱。","locateEn":"The Republican-penned order not only eliminated the strict net neutrality rules the FCC had adopted when it had a Democratic majority in 2015, but rejected the commission's authority to require broadband providers to do much of anything. The order also declared that state and local governments couldn't regulate broadband providers either.","locateZh":"由共和党主笔的这份命令不仅废除了 FCC 在 2015 年民主党占多数时通过的严格网络中立规则，还否定了 FCC 自身要求宽带商做任何事的监管权。该命令还宣布州和地方政府也不能监管宽带商。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"sticks to an out-of-date order 暗示 FCC 坚守旧命令；但原文 eliminated the strict net neutrality rules the FCC had adopted when it had a Democratic majority in 2015 明确是\"废除旧规则\"，方向正好相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"三个动作（eliminated, rejected, declared ... couldn't regulate）方向一致，全指向 anti-regulatory 这一立场。","pairs":[{"orig":"eliminated the strict net neutrality rules","opt":"takes an anti-regulatory stance"},{"orig":"rejected the commission's authority to require broadband providers to do much of anything","opt":"takes an anti-regulatory stance"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"has issued a special resolution 描述 FCC 出了一份特别决议；原文有的是\"由共和党主笔的命令\"以党派投票通过，并非\"特别决议\"，且通过的内容是放弃监管，不是某种特殊议案。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"has allowed the states to intervene 说 FCC 允许各州介入；但 The order also declared that state and local governments couldn't regulate broadband providers either 明确说州和地方都不能监管，方向相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"What can be learned about AT&T from Paragraph 3?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It protects against unfair competition."},{"key":"B","text":"It engages in anti-competitive practices."},{"key":"C","text":"It is under the FCC's investigation."},{"key":"D","text":"It is in pursuit of quality service."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从第3段可以了解到关于AT&T的什么信息?","choicesZh":{"A":"它防止不公平竞争。","B":"它从事反竞争行为。","C":"它正在接受FCC的调查。","D":"它在追求优质服务。"},"analysis":{"type":"What can be learned about AT&T from Paragraph 3? 限定段落、问可获知的客观信息，本质是定段细节题，不是推断题。","parse":"What can be learned about AT&T from Paragraph 3? 是常规疑问句：learned about AT&T 是\"关于 AT&T 可获知的内容\"，from Paragraph 3 限定信息来源段。无陷阱。","locateEn":"The commission argued that other agencies would protect against anti-competitive behavior, such as a broadband-providing conglomerate like AT&T favoring its own video-streaming service at the expense of Netflix and Apple TV.","locateZh":"FCC 辩称，会有别的机构防止反竞争行为，比如像 AT&T 这种宽带集团偏袒自家流媒体服务、损害 Netflix 和 Apple TV 的利益。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"protects against unfair competition 说 AT&T 反不公平竞争；但原文 other agencies would protect against anti-competitive behavior 是\"其他机构\"做这件事，AT&T 反而正是不公平竞争的实施者。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文用 such as 把\"反竞争行为\"具体化为 AT&T 的偏袒动作——也就是说 AT&T 正在进行反竞争行为，恰好是 engages in anti-competitive practices。","pairs":[{"orig":"anti-competitive behavior, such as a broadband-providing conglomerate like AT&T favoring its own video-streaming service at the expense of Netflix and Apple TV","opt":"engages in anti-competitive practices"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"It is under the FCC's investigation 说 AT&T 正受 FCC 调查；但 the FCC also ended the investigations of broadband providers that imposed data caps on their rivals' streaming services but not their own 说的是 FCC 终止了对那些设流量上限宽带商的调查，且原文没有点 AT&T 被调查，方向反且无依据。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"in pursuit of quality service 说 AT&T 追求高质量服务；但原文只提它偏袒自家流媒体（favoring its own video-streaming service），没说高质量，更是用作反面教材，不是赞扬。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"Judge Patricia Millett argues that the appeals court's decision____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"focus on trivialities."},{"key":"B","text":"conveys an ambiguous message."},{"key":"C","text":"is at odds with its earlier rulings."},{"key":"D","text":"is out of touch with reality."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"法官Patricia Millett认为上诉法院的裁决____","choicesZh":{"A":"关注琐碎小事。","B":"传达了一个模糊的信息。","C":"与其早期裁决相矛盾。","D":"脱离现实。"},"analysis":{"type":"Judge Patricia Millett argues that the appeals court's decision____ 要复述 Millett 的明确观点，原文有逐字引语，属客观信息抽取，非主观推断。","parse":"Judge Patricia Millett argues that the appeals court's decision____：主句主语 Judge Patricia Millett，谓语 argues，其后是 that 宾语从句；空格补的是从句的谓语，即\"上诉法院的决定怎么样\"。结构无陷阱，但要警惕\"是谁说的\"——这是 Millett 的话，不是法院本身的话。","locateEn":"But Judge Patricia Millett rightly argued in a concurring opinion that \"the result is unhinged from the realities of modern broadband service,\" and said Congress or the Supreme Court could intervene to \"avoid trapping Internet regulation in technological anachronism.\"","locateZh":"但 Millett 法官在协同意见中说得对：\"这一结果脱离了现代宽带服务的现实\"，并表示国会或最高法院可以介入，\"以免把互联网监管困在技术时代错置之中\"。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"focus on trivialities 说判决只盯小事；但 Millett 的批评是\"脱离现实\"而非\"专注琐事\"——severity 和 focus 维度都不同。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"conveys an ambiguous message 说判决传递的信息模糊；但 Millett 的评价 unhinged from the realities 是明确的\"脱离现实\"判定，并非说判决本身意思含糊。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"is at odds with its earlier rulings 说判决与法院早先裁定相互矛盾；但 the appeals court unanimously upheld the 2017 order ... citing a Supreme Court ruling from 2005 that upheld a similarly deregulatory move 反而说本次判决与 2005 年的裁定方向一致（都是去监管），不是矛盾；Millett 也没批评判决与早先裁定不符。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判说\"脱节\"，out of touch with reality 就是这层意思的标准英语表达——锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"the result is unhinged from the realities of modern broadband service","opt":"is out of touch with reality"}]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"What does the author argue in the last paragraph?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Congress needs to take action to ensure net neutrality."},{"key":"B","text":"The FCC should be put under strict supervision."},{"key":"C","text":"Rules need to be set to diversify online services."},{"key":"D","text":"Broadband providers' rights should be protected."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"作者在最后一段中论证了什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"国会需要采取行动以确保网络中立性。","B":"FCC应该被置于严格监督之下。","C":"需要制定规则以使在线服务多样化。","D":"宽带提供商的权利应该受到保护。"},"analysis":{"type":"What does the author argue in the last paragraph? 问的是末段所表达的作者主张，而非某细节——属于局部主旨题，要把 P6 的功能与全文走向串起来判断。","parse":"What does the author argue in the last paragraph? 是 wh- 一般疑问：author 是主语，argue 是谓语，in the last paragraph 限定范围。结构平铺无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判说\"国会立法保网络中立\"，Congress needs to take action to ensure net neutrality 是一字不差的同义表达，锁 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"cry out for Congress to act","opt":"Congress needs to take action to ensure net neutrality"},{"orig":"create clear rules protecting openness and innovation online","opt":"to ensure net neutrality"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"The FCC should be put under strict supervision 说应该对 FCC 严加监督；但末段 It needs to give the commission explicit authority 说的是\"应给 FCC 明确授权\"——是赋权，不是监督。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Rules need to be set to diversify online services 说立规则要多样化在线服务；但末段 protecting openness and innovation online 强调的是\"保护开放与创新\"，并非\"多样化服务\"——目的不同。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Broadband providers' rights should be protected 主张保护宽带商权利；但全文从 P1 到 P6 一路批评宽带商可能偏袒自家、举 AT&T 为反竞争例证，末段更要 bar broadband providers from meddling in the traffic——是限权，不是保护其权利。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"matching","title":"Section II Part B 选句填空","directions":"Directions: In the following text, some sentences have been removed. For Questions 41-45, choose the most suitable one from the list A-G to fit into each of the numbered blanks. There are two extra choices, which do not fit in any of the blanks. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"","text":"In the movies and on television, artificial intelligence is typically depicted as something sinister that will upend our way of life. When it comes to AI in business, we often hear about it in relation to automation and the impending loss of jobs, but in what ways is AI changing companies and the larger economy that don't involve doom-and-gloom mass unemployment predictions?"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"","text":"A recent survey of manufacturing and service industries from Tata Consultancy Services found that companies currently use AI more often in computer-to-computer activities than in automating human activities. Here are a few ways AI is aiding companies without replacing employees:"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"","text":"Better hiring practices"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"","text":"Companies are using artificial intelligence to remove some of the unconscious bias from hiring decisions. \"There are experiments that show that, naturally, the results of interviews are much more biased than what AI does,\" says Pedro Domingos, author of The Master Algorithm: How the Quest for the Ultimate Learning Machine Will Remake Our World and a computer science professor at the University of Washington. \" {{41}} \" One company that's doing this is called Blendoor. It uses analytics to help identify where there may be bias in the hiring process."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"","text":"More effective marketing"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"","text":"Some AI software can analyze and optimize marketing email subject lines to increase open rates. One company in the UK, Phrasee, claims their software can outperform humans by up to 10 percent when it comes to email open rates. This can mean millions more in revenue. {{42}} These are \"tools that help people use data, not a replacement for people,\" says Patrick H. Winston, a professor of artificial intelligence and computer science at MIT."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-7","label":"","text":"Saving customers money"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-8","label":"","text":"Energy companies can use AI to help customers reduce their electricity bills, saving them money while helping the environment. Companies can also optimize their own energy use and cut down on the cost of electricity. Insurance companies, meanwhile, can base their premiums on AI models that more accurately assess risk. Domingos says, \" {{43}} \""},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-9","label":"","text":"Improved accuracy"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-10","label":"","text":"\"Machine learning often provides a more reliable form of statistics which makes data more valuable,\" says Winston. It \"helps people make smarter decisions.\" {{44}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-11","label":"","text":"Protecting and maintaining infrastructure"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-12","label":"","text":"A number of companies, particularly in energy and transportation, use AI image processing technology to inspect infrastructure and prevent equipment failure or leaks before they happen. \"If they fail first and then you fix them, it's very expensive,\" says Domingos. \" {{45}} \""}]},"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"AI replaces the boring parts of your job. If you're doing research, you can have AI go out and look for relevant sources and information that otherwise you just wouldn't have time for."},{"key":"B","text":"One accounting firm, BY, uses an AI system that helps review contracts during an audit. This process, along with employees reviewing the contracts, is faster and more accurate."},{"key":"C","text":"There are also companies like Acquisio, which analyzes advertising performance across multiple channels like Adwords, Bing and social media and makes adjustments or suggestions about where advertising funds will yield best results."},{"key":"D","text":"You want to predict if something needs attention now and point to where it's useful for employees to go to."},{"key":"E","text":"Before, they might not insure the ones who felt like a high risk or charge them too much, or they would charge them too little and then it would cost the company money."},{"key":"F","text":"We're also giving our customers better channels versus picking up the phone to accomplish something beyond human scale."},{"key":"G","text":"AI looks at resumes in greater numbers than humans would be able to, and selects the more promising candidates."}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AI replaces the boring parts of your job. If you're doing research, you can have AI go out and look for relevant sources and information that otherwise you just wouldn't have time for."},{"key":"B","text":"One accounting firm, BY, uses an AI system that helps review contracts during an audit. This process, along with employees reviewing the contracts, is faster and more accurate."},{"key":"C","text":"There are also companies like Acquisio, which analyzes advertising performance across multiple channels like Adwords, Bing and social media and makes adjustments or suggestions about where advertising funds will yield best results."},{"key":"D","text":"You want to predict if something needs attention now and point to where it's useful for employees to go to."},{"key":"E","text":"Before, they might not insure the ones who felt like a high risk or charge them too much, or they would charge them too little and then it would cost the company money."},{"key":"F","text":"We're also giving our customers better channels versus picking up the phone to accomplish something beyond human scale."},{"key":"G","text":"AI looks at resumes in greater numbers than humans would be able to, and selects the more promising candidates."}],"answer":"G","explanation":{"answer":"G","type":"段中","stemZh":"41. (41)____","reason":"AI looks at resumes in greater numbers than humans would be able to, and selects the more promising candidates. 人工智能审阅的简历数量超过人类所能处理的数量,并筛选出更有希望的候选人。\n夹在专家引语中间，须补一句仍在讲\"AI 减少招聘偏见\"的话 空前是 Domingos 的话 the results of interviews are much more biased than what AI does，说\"面试比 AI 更带偏见\"；空本身用引号独立成句、仍在引语内；空后立刻举例 One company that's doing this is called Blendoor.。本段小标题是\"更好的招聘做法\"。所以这个空要补一句\"承接前面 AI 比人更少偏见、进一步说 AI 在招聘里具体怎么做\"的话，好让后面的 Blendoor 例子有 this 可指。\n话题对上招聘、且正好做了 this 的先行词 looks at resumes in greater numbers than humans would be able to, and selects the more promising candidates 句句扣招聘（简历、候选人），与小标题 Better hiring practices 严丝合缝；它描述的正是\"AI 海量筛简历挑人\"这件事，恰好给空后 One company that's doing this 的 this 提供了着落——Blendoor 做的就是这件事。前后双向缝合。","options":{},"choiceEn":"AI looks at resumes in greater numbers than humans would be able to, and selects the more promising candidates.","clues":["结构功能 本段话题被小标题锁死在\"招聘\" 小标题 Better hiring practices 与段内 remove some of the unconscious bias from hiring decisions 把整段话题限定在招聘，所填句必须仍在讲\"AI 与招聘\"，而不能岔到别的业务。","代词指代 空后 this 需要先行词 空后紧接 One company that's doing this is called Blendoor.，其中 this 指代\"AI 在招聘里做的某件事\"，要求所填句正是描述\"AI 具体怎么处理简历/候选人\"这件可被 this 回指的事。"]}},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AI replaces the boring parts of your job. If you're doing research, you can have AI go out and look for relevant sources and information that otherwise you just wouldn't have time for."},{"key":"B","text":"One accounting firm, BY, uses an AI system that helps review contracts during an audit. This process, along with employees reviewing the contracts, is faster and more accurate."},{"key":"C","text":"There are also companies like Acquisio, which analyzes advertising performance across multiple channels like Adwords, Bing and social media and makes adjustments or suggestions about where advertising funds will yield best results."},{"key":"D","text":"You want to predict if something needs attention now and point to where it's useful for employees to go to."},{"key":"E","text":"Before, they might not insure the ones who felt like a high risk or charge them too much, or they would charge them too little and then it would cost the company money."},{"key":"F","text":"We're also giving our customers better channels versus picking up the phone to accomplish something beyond human scale."},{"key":"G","text":"AI looks at resumes in greater numbers than humans would be able to, and selects the more promising candidates."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"段中","stemZh":"42. (42)____","reason":"There are also companies like Acquisio, which analyzes advertising performance across multiple channels like Adwords, Bing and social media and makes adjustments or suggestions about where advertising funds will yield best results. 还有像Acquisio这样的公司,它分析Adwords、Bing和社交媒体等多个渠道的广告效果,并就广告资金投放到哪里会产生最佳效果做出调整或提出建议。\n夹在两个营销例子之间，须补一个\"再举一个营销工具\"的并列例子 空前讲 One company in the UK, Phrasee, claims their software can outperform humans by up to 10 percent 这一营销邮件优化的例子；空后是专家总评 These are \"tools that help people use data, not a replacement for people\"，用复数 These 指代\"前面这些工具\"。本段小标题是\"更有效的营销\"。所以空里要补\"与 Phrasee 并列的又一个营销类 AI 工具例子\"，这样空后的复数 These 才有不止一个例子可指。\nalso 递进 + 营销话题，正好凑成 These 的复数 There are also companies like Acquisio 的 also 表\"再举一个同类例子\"，紧承前面的 Phrasee；内容 analyzes advertising performance across multiple channels 牢牢扣住营销，与小标题 More effective marketing 一致；它与 Phrasee 一起，正好让空后复数 These are 有两个工具可指，缝合上下文。","options":{},"choiceEn":"There are also companies like Acquisio, which analyzes advertising performance across multiple channels like Adwords, Bing and social media and makes adjustments or suggestions about where advertising funds will yield best results.","clues":["结构功能 本段话题被小标题锁死在\"营销\" 小标题 More effective marketing 与段内 optimize marketing email subject lines 把整段锁在营销，所填句必须是营销类的 AI 工具/公司，不能岔题。","代词指代 空后 These 是复数，需多个例子作先行 空后 These are \"tools that help people use data, not a replacement for people\" 用复数 These 总指前文工具；空前只出现 Phrasee 一个，复数要求空里再补一个同类工具，才凑得齐 These 所指。"]}},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AI replaces the boring parts of your job. If you're doing research, you can have AI go out and look for relevant sources and information that otherwise you just wouldn't have time for."},{"key":"B","text":"One accounting firm, BY, uses an AI system that helps review contracts during an audit. This process, along with employees reviewing the contracts, is faster and more accurate."},{"key":"C","text":"There are also companies like Acquisio, which analyzes advertising performance across multiple channels like Adwords, Bing and social media and makes adjustments or suggestions about where advertising funds will yield best results."},{"key":"D","text":"You want to predict if something needs attention now and point to where it's useful for employees to go to."},{"key":"E","text":"Before, they might not insure the ones who felt like a high risk or charge them too much, or they would charge them too little and then it would cost the company money."},{"key":"F","text":"We're also giving our customers better channels versus picking up the phone to accomplish something beyond human scale."},{"key":"G","text":"AI looks at resumes in greater numbers than humans would be able to, and selects the more promising candidates."}],"answer":"E","explanation":{"answer":"E","type":"段末","stemZh":"43. (43)____","reason":"Before, they might not insure the ones who felt like a high risk or charge them too much, or they would charge them too little and then it would cost the company money. 以前,他们可能不会为那些感觉风险高的人投保或向他们收取过高费用,或者他们会收费过低,然后给公司造成损失。\n段末引语空，须补 Domingos 一句承接\"AI 让保险定价更准\"的话 空前末句 Insurance companies, meanwhile, can base their premiums on AI models that more accurately assess risk. 说\"保险公司能用 AI 模型更准确评估风险来定保费\"，随后本段以 Domingos says, \"__(43)__\" 收尾——空嵌在引语之中、且是本段最后一句。本段小标题是\"为客户省钱\"。所以空里要补 Domingos 一句\"具体说明 AI 定价为何更准、或过去定价怎么不准\"的话，与前面\"更准确评估风险\"接上。\nBefore 接上\"现在更准\"、they 指保险公司、词域全复现 Before, they might not insure the ones who felt like a high risk or charge them too much, or they would charge them too little and then it would cost the company money：句首 Before 与前句\"现在 AI 更准\"构成今昔对比；they 回指前句 Insurance companies；insure、high risk、charge 全面复现保险定价话题，正是\"过去评估不准会拒保/收太高或太低\"的反面，把\"AI 更准\"的价值讲透。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Before, they might not insure the ones who felt like a high risk or charge them too much, or they would charge them too little and then it would cost the company money.","clues":["词汇复现 前句\"risk / insurance / premiums\"须在空里复现 空前 Insurance companies, meanwhile, can base their premiums on AI models that more accurately assess risk 反复出现保险、保费、风险；所填句很可能再次出现 insure/risk/charge 这类同域词，把\"更准确评估风险\"的好处具体化。","逻辑连接 前句讲\"现在更准\"，空里宜以\"过去不准\"作对比 前句强调 more accurately assess risk——\"现在\"更准；按今昔对比的常见写法，所填句宜补\"过去定价不准会怎样\"，用反面衬托 AI 带来的改进。"]}},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AI replaces the boring parts of your job. If you're doing research, you can have AI go out and look for relevant sources and information that otherwise you just wouldn't have time for."},{"key":"B","text":"One accounting firm, BY, uses an AI system that helps review contracts during an audit. This process, along with employees reviewing the contracts, is faster and more accurate."},{"key":"C","text":"There are also companies like Acquisio, which analyzes advertising performance across multiple channels like Adwords, Bing and social media and makes adjustments or suggestions about where advertising funds will yield best results."},{"key":"D","text":"You want to predict if something needs attention now and point to where it's useful for employees to go to."},{"key":"E","text":"Before, they might not insure the ones who felt like a high risk or charge them too much, or they would charge them too little and then it would cost the company money."},{"key":"F","text":"We're also giving our customers better channels versus picking up the phone to accomplish something beyond human scale."},{"key":"G","text":"AI looks at resumes in greater numbers than humans would be able to, and selects the more promising candidates."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"段末","stemZh":"44. (44)____","reason":"One accounting firm, BY, uses an AI system that helps review contracts during an audit. This process, along with employees reviewing the contracts, is faster and more accurate. 一家会计师事务所BY使用一个人工智能系统,在审计期间帮助审查合同。这一过程连同员工审查合同,速度更快且更准确。\n段末空须补一个\"AI 提升准确性\"的具体实例 空前是 Winston 的两句话 Machine learning often provides a more reliable form of statistics which makes data more valuable 和 helps people make smarter decisions.，都是抽象论点；空在本段末尾。本段小标题是\"提升准确性\"。论点已抛却没给实例，所以段末这个空要补一个\"AI 让数据更可靠/决策更准\"的具体例子来收尾。\n会计所审合同实例、more accurate 直接复现 One accounting firm, BY, uses an AI system that helps review contracts during an audit 是\"One + 公司\"的落地实例，正好给前面抽象论点配例；句末 faster and more accurate 直接复现小标题 Improved accuracy 与 a more reliable form of statistics；并且 along with employees reviewing the contracts 强调\"连同员工一起\"，呼应全文\"帮人不替人\"基调，作段末收尾恰当。","options":{},"choiceEn":"One accounting firm, BY, uses an AI system that helps review contracts during an audit. This process, along with employees reviewing the contracts, is faster and more accurate.","clues":["结构功能 本段话题被小标题锁死在\"准确\" 小标题 Improved accuracy 与段内 a more reliable form of statistics 把话题锁在\"更可靠/更准确\"，所填句必须围绕\"准确性\"，且最好是个落地实例。","词汇复现 前文\"reliable / smarter decisions\"应在空里有同义复现 前句 a more reliable form of statistics、helps people make smarter decisions 强调可靠与更明智，所填实例宜出现 accurate/faster 这类同义词，把抽象的\"更准\"具体化。"]}},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AI replaces the boring parts of your job. If you're doing research, you can have AI go out and look for relevant sources and information that otherwise you just wouldn't have time for."},{"key":"B","text":"One accounting firm, BY, uses an AI system that helps review contracts during an audit. This process, along with employees reviewing the contracts, is faster and more accurate."},{"key":"C","text":"There are also companies like Acquisio, which analyzes advertising performance across multiple channels like Adwords, Bing and social media and makes adjustments or suggestions about where advertising funds will yield best results."},{"key":"D","text":"You want to predict if something needs attention now and point to where it's useful for employees to go to."},{"key":"E","text":"Before, they might not insure the ones who felt like a high risk or charge them too much, or they would charge them too little and then it would cost the company money."},{"key":"F","text":"We're also giving our customers better channels versus picking up the phone to accomplish something beyond human scale."},{"key":"G","text":"AI looks at resumes in greater numbers than humans would be able to, and selects the more promising candidates."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"段末","stemZh":"45. (45)____","reason":"You want to predict if something needs attention now and point to where it's useful for employees to go to. 你想预测某件事现在是否需要关注,并指出员工去哪里有用。\nDomingos 引语收尾，须补一句\"应提前预测、防患于未然\"的话 空前 Domingos 说 If they fail first and then you fix them, it's very expensive，强调\"等坏了再修很贵\"；空紧随其后、独立成引语、且全段全文到此结束。本段小标题是\"保护与维护基础设施\"，段内讲 inspect infrastructure and prevent equipment failure or leaks before they happen。所以空里要补 Domingos 一句\"与其坏了再修、不如提前预测哪里要出问题\"的对策性收尾话。\npredict now 正是\"坏了再修\"的反面对策 You want to predict if something needs attention now and point to where it's useful for employees to go to：predict if something needs attention now 与前句 If they fail first and then you fix them, it's very expensive 构成\"事前预测 vs 事后补救\"的对照，正是 Domingos 要给的对策；\"现在就预测哪里需关注\"复现段内 before they happen 的事前精神；point to where it's useful for employees to go to 指引员工，呼应\"帮人不替人\"，收尾贴切。","options":{},"choiceEn":"You want to predict if something needs attention now and point to where it's useful for employees to go to.","clues":["逻辑连接 前句讲\"坏了再修很贵\"，空里应给\"提前应对\"的反面对策 前句 If they fail first and then you fix them, it's very expensive 是\"事后补救代价高\"的反面；按对照逻辑，所填句应给出\"事前预测、防患未然\"的正面做法。","词汇复现 段内\"prevent ... before they happen\"应在空里以\"预测\"复现 段内 prevent equipment failure or leaks before they happen 的核心是\"事前\"，所填句宜复现\"预测/现在就关注\"这层意思，呼应\"在故障发生前巡检\"。"]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"World War II was the watershed event for higher education in modern Western societies. (46) Those societies came out of the war with levels of enrollment that had been roughly constant at 3-5% of the relevant age groups during the decades before the war. But after the war, great social and political changes arising out of the successful war against Fascism created a growing demand in European and American economies for increasing numbers of graduates with more than a secondary school education. (47) And the demand that rose in those societies for entry to higher education extended to groups and social classes that had not thought of attending a university before the war. These demands resulted in a very rapid expansion of the systems of higher education, beginning in the 1960s and developing very rapidly (though unevenly) during the 1970s and 1980s."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"The growth of higher education manifests itself in at least three quite different ways, and these in turn have given rise to different sets of problems. There was first the rate of growth: (48) in many countries of Western Europe, the numbers of students in higher education doubled within five-year periods during the 1960s and doubled again in seven, eight, or 10 years by the middle of the 1970s. Second, growth obviously affected the absolute size both of systems and individual institutions. And third, growth was reflected in changes in the proportion of the relevant age group enrolled in institutions of higher education."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-3","text":"Each of these manifestations of growth carried its own peculiar problems in its wake. For example, a high growth rate placed great strains on the existing structures of governance, of administration, and above all of socialization. When a faculty or department grows from, say, five to 20 members within three or four years, (49) and when the new staff are predominantly young men and women fresh from postgraduate study, they largely define the norms of academic life in that faculty. And if the postgraduate student population also grows rapidly and there is loss of a close apprenticeship relationship between faculty members and students, the student culture becomes the chief socializing force for new postgraduate students, with consequences for the intellectual and academic life of the institution-this was seen in America as well as in France, Italy, West Germany, and Japan. (50) High growth rates increased the chances for academic innovation; they also weakened the forms and processes by which teachers and students are admitted into a community of scholars during periods of stability or slow growth. In the 1960s and 1970s, European universities saw marked changes in their governance arrangements, with empowerment of junior faculty and to some degree of students as well."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"Those societies came out of the war with levels of enrollment that had been roughly constant at 3-5% of the relevant age groups during the decades before the war.","refZh":"在二战前的几十年里，这些（西方）社会的高校入学率一直大致稳定在适龄人口的 3-5%，二战结束时仍维持着这一水平。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Those societies came out of the war","lit":"那些社会走出了战争","role":"（主干主谓 + 介词短语）","note":"难点： Those societies 需回指 + come out of 取「结束/走出」义 Those societies 必须回到 World War II was the watershed event for higher education in modern Western societies. 才能锁定为「西方（这些）社会」；come out of the war 不是「从战争里出来」字面义，而是「（这些社会）二战结束时」的时间标记，主体考生若直译会很别扭，应汉化为「战争结束时」或「从二战中走出来时」。"},{"en":"with levels of enrollment","lit":"带着入学率水平","role":"（with 引导的伴随状语（介词短语））","note":"难点： enrollment 在高教语境取「入学率/录取人数」 enrollment 直译「登记/注册」不合本文，结合 demand in European and American economies for increasing numbers of graduates 的高教语境，此处统一译为「（高校）入学率」或「在校生比例」。"},{"en":"that had been roughly constant at 3-5% of the relevant age groups","lit":"那（入学率）大致稳定地保持在相关年龄群体的 3-5%","role":"（定语从句（修饰 levels of enrollment））","note":"难点： 过去完成时 + roughly constant + relevant age groups 三处都易丢分 had been constant 是过去完成时，强调「战前几十年里一直保持」；roughly 是程度限定词「大致」，不可漏；relevant age groups 指「相应年龄段的人口」即适龄人口，直译「相关的年龄群体」不通顺，应具体化为「适龄人口」或「相应年龄段人口」。"},{"en":"during the decades before the war.","lit":"在战前的几十年间","role":"（时间状语）","note":"难点： the decades 不是「几十年」，是「战前那几十年」 the 是特指，结合上文 World War II was the watershed event，此处指「二战之前的那几十年」；翻译时把时间状语提前到句首，更符合汉语习惯。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"And the demand that rose in those societies for entry to higher education extended to groups and social classes that had not thought of attending a university before the war.","refZh":"而在这些社会中兴起的对接受高等教育的需求，也波及到了一些群体和社会阶层——这些人在战前从未想过要上大学。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"And the demand","lit":"（而）这种需求","role":"（主语（带连词 And））","note":""},{"en":"that rose in those societies for entry to higher education","lit":"在那些社会中兴起的、要求进入高等教育的（需求）","role":"（定语从句 1（修饰 the demand））","note":"难点： rose 取「兴起/产生」义 + for entry to higher education 是介词短语补足 demand 的对象 rose 不是「上升」而是「兴起、产生」，因为主语是 demand 这种抽象事物；for entry to higher education 是介词短语，紧跟 demand 表达「对……的需求」，而不是修饰 those societies；主体考生易把 for 误挂到 societies 上，造成结构错乱。entry 在此为「进入（高校）」之义，可具体化为「上大学／接受高等教育」。"},{"en":"extended to groups and social classes","lit":"扩展到（一些）群体和社会阶层","role":"（主干谓语 + 宾语）","note":"难点： extended to 译「波及/蔓延到」更贴汉语 extended to 字面「扩展到」尚可，但在「需求蔓延到某类人群」的语境里译成「波及/蔓延到/惠及」更符合汉语；social classes 译「社会阶层」是固定术语，不要译成「社会等级/社会阶级」（后者带政治色彩，与原文中性社会学描述不符）。"},{"en":"that had not thought of attending a university before the war.","lit":"（这些群体和阶层）在战前从未想过要上大学","role":"（定语从句 2（修饰 groups and social classes））","note":"难点： 过去完成时 had not thought of + before the war 双重时间锁定 had not thought of 是过去完成时，与 before the war 配合，强调「战前从未有过这个念头」；不可漏译「从未/根本没」这种语气；think of doing 是固定搭配「想过做……」，译成「想过上大学/想到要读大学」即可。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"in many countries of Western Europe, the numbers of students in higher education doubled within five-year periods during the 1960s and doubled again in seven, eight, or 10 years by the middle of the 1970s.","refZh":"在西欧许多国家，接受高等教育的学生人数在 20 世纪 60 年代每五年就翻一番，到 70 年代中期，又用了七、八或十年时间再翻了一番。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"in many countries of Western Europe,","lit":"在西欧许多国家","role":"（地点状语）","note":"难点： Western Europe 是固定地理名词「西欧」 Western Europe 必须译成「西欧」而非「西部欧洲」；考研一对地理/历史专名要求精准，多个 of countries of Western Europe = 西欧的许多国家。"},{"en":"the numbers of students in higher education","lit":"高等教育中的学生人数","role":"（主语（含介词短语后置定语））","note":"难点： the numbers of students = 学生人数（注意复数+定冠词的整体性） the numbers of students 是「学生人数」整体，in higher education 是后置介词短语作定语，译成「（接受）高等教育的学生人数」或「高校在校生人数」；汉化时把后置介词短语前移译「的」。"},{"en":"doubled within five-year periods during the 1960s","lit":"在 20 世纪 60 年代每五年就翻一番","role":"（谓语 1 + 时间状语）","note":"难点： double 作动词「翻一番」+ within five-year periods 表「每五年内」 double 作动词意为「翻一番/翻倍」，主体考生易译成「加倍」其实不准；within five-year periods 中 periods 用复数，暗含「一个又一个五年周期内」即「每五年」；the 1960s 是「20 世纪 60 年代」，「19」不可省略。"},{"en":"and doubled again in seven, eight, or 10 years","lit":"并在七、八或十年内再次翻一番","role":"（谓语 2（and 并列））","note":"难点： doubled again 是「又翻了一番」+ in seven, eight, or 10 years 表所需时间 again 提示「第二次翻番」，速度比上次略慢（7~10 年才翻一番，而上面是 5 年）；in seven, eight, or 10 years 中 in 表「在……时间内」，表达完成翻番所用的时间长度。"},{"en":"by the middle of the 1970s.","lit":"到 20 世纪 70 年代中期","role":"（时间状语（截止时间））","note":"难点： by 表「到……为止」的截止时间 by 不是 in/at，它表「到某时为止（这件事已发生）」，必须译出「到……（之前/中期）」的截止意味；the middle of the 1970s = 20 世纪 70 年代中期。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"and when the new staff are predominantly young men and women fresh from postgraduate study, they largely define the norms of academic life in that faculty.","refZh":"而当这些新进教职员工绝大多数都是刚出研究生院的年轻男女时，他们就在很大程度上塑造了该院系的学风。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"and when the new staff are predominantly young men and women","lit":"并且当新教职员工大多是年轻的男女","role":"（时间/条件状语从句（when 引导））","note":"难点： predominantly 译「绝大多数/主要是」+ staff 集合名词译「教职员工」 predominantly 是高频副词，意为「主要地、大部分地」，本处译「绝大多数是」最贴切，不要漏译这个程度副词（采分点）；the new staff 在大学语境里特指「新进的教职员工」，不是「员工」泛指；when 在此引导「时间+条件」复合状语从句，对应汉语「当……时」。"},{"en":"fresh from postgraduate study,","lit":"刚从研究生学习中走出来的","role":"（形容词短语作后置定语（修饰 young men and women））","note":"难点： fresh from = 「刚刚从……出来」固定搭配 fresh 不是「新鲜的」字面义，fresh from sth 是固定搭配「刚从某处出来 / 刚结束某事」，本处指「刚读完研究生」即「刚出研究生院的」；postgraduate study 译「研究生阶段学习」或「读研」；这块作为后置定语修饰 young men and women，汉化时前置译「刚出研究生院的（年轻男女）」。"},{"en":"they largely define the norms of academic life","lit":"他们在很大程度上界定学术生活的规范","role":"（主干主谓宾）","note":"难点： they 必须回指为「这些新教职」+ define 译「界定/塑造」+ norms 译「规范/准则」 they 必须回到本句前半 the new staff are predominantly young men and women fresh from postgraduate study 锁定为「这些新教职」或「他们」（紧贴前半时可保留「他们」）；largely 是程度副词「很大程度上/主要地」，采分点不可漏；define the norms 字面「定义规范」，更地道的译法是「塑造规范、奠定准则」；norms of academic life = 学术生活的（行为）规范、学风。"},{"en":"in that faculty.","lit":"在那个院系中","role":"（地点状语（介词短语））","note":"难点： faculty 此处取「院系/系」义，不是「能力/教员」 faculty 是考研一高频熟词僻义词：①「能力」②「全体教员」③「（大学的）系/学院」。结合上文 When a faculty or department grows from, say, five to 20 members，本处与 department 并列，明确指「院系」；that faculty = 那个院系，特指上文提到的扩张中的院系。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"High growth rates increased the chances for academic innovation; they also weakened the forms and processes by which teachers and students are admitted into a community of scholars during periods of stability or slow growth.","refZh":"高增长率增加了学术革新的机会；但与此同时，它也削弱了（旧有的）那些形式与过程——也就是稳定或缓慢增长时期，教师和学生被接纳进学者共同体所依靠的方式和流程。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"High growth rates increased the chances for academic innovation;","lit":"高增长率增加了学术革新的机会","role":"（分号前独立主句 1）","note":"难点： growth rates 译「增长率」+ academic innovation 译「学术革新/学术创新」 High growth rates 紧接上文 a high growth rate placed great strains on the existing structures 即「（高等教育的）高速增长率/扩张速度」；chances for 译「……的机会」；academic innovation 是「学术革新/学术创新」固定术语，不要译成「学院创新」。分号在英文里是并列两个独立句，汉语里译成「；」或拆成两句皆可。"},{"en":"they also weakened the forms and processes","lit":"它们也削弱了（某些）方式和过程","role":"（分号后独立主句 2 的主干）","note":"难点： they 必须回指为「高增长率」+ also 表「同时也」转折语气 they 紧贴分号前的 High growth rates，主体考生必须把 they 回指为「（这种）高增长率」，否则译成「它们」会指代悬空；also 与前句呼应，表「同时也带来负面后果」，承接语气不可漏（采分点）；the forms and processes 译「形式与过程」或「方式与流程」，配合下文定从理解为「（接纳新人进入学术圈的）程序」。"},{"en":"by which teachers and students are admitted into a community of scholars","lit":"通过这些方式和过程，教师和学生被接纳进一个学者共同体","role":"（定语从句（修饰 the forms and processes））","note":"难点： by which 引导方式定从 + be admitted into = 被接纳进 + community of scholars = 学者共同体 by which 是「介词+关系代词」结构，by 表方式，还原为 by the forms and processes（通过这些方式和过程）；are admitted into 是被动语态，汉译为主动「（教师和学生）加入/进入」或保留「被接纳进」；a community of scholars 是术语，译「学者共同体/学术共同体」，体现一种学术身份归属。"},{"en":"during periods of stability or slow growth.","lit":"在稳定或缓慢增长的时期","role":"（时间状语）","note":"难点： during periods of ... 表「在……时期」+ stability or slow growth 并列 during periods of stability or slow growth 直译为「在稳定或缓慢增长的时期」，意指「与本句开头的『高增长』形成对比的（旧时代）稳定/慢增长时期」；这是一个隐性对比，译文要让读者感到「这套程序原本只在稳定时期管用，而高增长把它打破了」。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: A foreign friend of yours has recently graduated from college and intends to find a job in China. Write him/her an email to make some suggestions . You should write about 100 words on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not sign your own name at the end. Use “Li Ming” instead. Do not write the address. ( 10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: A foreign friend of yours has recently graduated from college and intends to find a job in China. Write him/her an email to make some suggestions . You should write about 100 words on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not sign your own name at the end. Use “Li Ming” instead. Do not write the address. ( 10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"Dear Chris, Congratulations on your graduation! I'm delighted that you plan to look for a job here in China, and I'd love to offer a few suggestions. First, it would help to learn more about China's job market and improve your Chinese, since good language skills make daily work far easier. Second, why not register on popular recruiting websites and reach out to your university's alumni? They often share useful openings. Finally, prepare a clear resume and rehearse for interviews in advance. If you need any help with your job hunt, just let me know. Best wishes, Li Ming","translation":"亲爱的克里斯：\n祝贺你毕业！得知你打算在中国找工作，我很高兴，也很想给你几点建议。\n第一，多了解一下中国的就业市场、并提高你的中文水平会很有帮助，因为良好的语言能力能让日常工作轻松得多。第二，何不在热门招聘网站上注册，并联系你母校的校友呢？他们常会分享有用的招聘信息。最后，提前准备一份清晰的简历，并演练面试。\n如果你在求职中需要任何帮助，尽管告诉我。\n顺祝一切顺利 李明","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"称呼落地","text":"【第 1 段】 称呼落地 。用『Dear Chris,』顶格，直接以名字称呼锁定朋友语气，落实 outline 第1块。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"祝贺+来意","text":"【第 2 段】 祝贺+来意 。『Congratulations on your graduation!』道贺拉近距离，『I'd love to offer a few suggestions』一句点明写信来意。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"分条给建议","text":"【第 3 段】 分条给建议 。用『First』『Second』『Finally』串起三条针对在华求职的具体建议，每条都是可操作动作，落实分条方法。"},{"tag":"【第 4 段】","core":"提供帮助收尾","text":"【第 4 段】 提供帮助收尾 。『If you need any help with your job hunt, just let me know.』主动伸手，完成交际闭环。"},{"tag":"【第 5 段】","core":"规定署名","text":"【第 5 段】 规定署名 。『Best wishes,』接另起一行的『Li Ming』，满足不署真名、改用 Li Ming 的硬约束。"}],"wordCount":99}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160 - 200 words based on the following picture. In your essay, you should 1) describe the picture briefly, 2) interpret its intended meaning, and 3) give your comments. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160 - 200 words based on the following picture. In your essay, you should 1) describe the picture briefly, 2) interpret its intended meaning, and 3) give your comments. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2021-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"画中左侧是一个装扮成美猴王的小孩，右手还拿着一根小棒子","width":"1024","height":"1024","local":"assets/writing/2021-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is vividly depicted in the cartoon, a little boy dressed up as the Monkey King, holding a small stick, is talking to his father. The boy says that many of his classmates think learning traditional opera is boring, while the father replies that as long as the boy himself enjoys it, that is enough. Simple as the picture is, it conveys a thought-provoking message about following one's own interest rather than blindly bowing to others' opinions. The father's answer reveals that genuine passion, not popular approval, should guide our choices. What's more, the child's love for opera mirrors a positive trend of young people embracing traditional culture, which deserves encouragement. Therefore, I firmly agree with the father's attitude. On the one hand, only when we stick to what we truly love can we find lasting motivation and happiness. On the other hand, respecting a child's own interest helps cultivate confident and independent individuals. In light of this, parents and society should learn to listen to children's inner voice instead of imposing mainstream standards. Only in this way can each unique talent blossom.","translation":"正如漫画生动描绘的，一个装扮成美猴王、手里还拿着小棒子的小男孩正在和父亲说话。孩子说他的许多同学觉得学传统戏曲很无聊，而父亲回答说，只要孩子自己喜欢，那就足够了。\n画面虽简单，却传递出一个发人深省的信息：要遵从自己内心的兴趣，而不是盲目屈从于他人的看法。父亲的回答揭示出，指引我们选择的应当是真正的热爱，而非大众的认可。更重要的是，孩子对戏曲的喜爱折射出年轻人拥抱传统文化的积极趋势，这值得鼓励。\n因此，我坚决赞同父亲的态度。一方面，只有坚持自己真正热爱的东西，我们才能找到持久的动力与快乐。另一方面，尊重孩子自己的兴趣有助于培养自信而独立的人。有鉴于此，父母和社会应学会倾听孩子内心的声音，而不是强加主流标准。唯有如此，每一份独特的才华才能绽放。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"白描画面落实描述任务","text":"【第 1 段】 白描画面落实描述任务 。本段用 As is vividly depicted in the cartoon 总起，再转述两句对话，一般现在时白描，两句话完成 describe the picture briefly，不拖泥带水。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"用 mirrors 把画面挂到现实","text":"【第 2 段】 用 mirrors 把画面挂到现实 。本段以 Simple as the picture is 让步过渡，用 reveals、mirrors 把父亲的话引申到‘热爱指引选择’与传统文化趋势，正是 interpret its intended meaning 要的引申。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"表态加对策完成评论","text":"【第 3 段】 表态加对策完成评论 。本段 Therefore 表态、On the one hand / On the other hand 给双理由、In light of this 给对策，落实 give your comments。"}],"wordCount":183}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 C peaks · 2 D generally · 3 A while · 4 B accumulation · 5 A possibility · 6 A delay · 7 C included · 8 B compared · 9 A with · 10 C scored · 11 D went by · 12 B attributable · 13 C involved · 14 D explain · 15 D treatments · 16 B Meanwhile · 17 D take · 18 A well-being · 19 A level · 20 C diet \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 C · 22 B · 23 C · 24 D · 25 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 B · 27 D · 28 C · 29 C · 30 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 A · 32 B · 33 D · 34 A · 35 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 C · 37 B · 38 B · 39 D · 40 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"选句填空（7选5） Section II Part B （41–45 题） 41 G · 42 C · 43 E · 44 B · 45 D \n（逐题解析见 选句填空（7选5）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":45,"missingSections":[]}};
